  <para style="h">Ñwed Mbon Rom</para>
  <para style="toc1">Ñwed Mbon Rom</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ñwed Mbon Rom</para>
  <para style="toc3">Rom</para>
  <para style="mt1">Ñwed Mbon Rom</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="ROM 1" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 1:1" />Pọọl, ayịnufọk Krais Yisọs, e-ekoodo nọ adido abọsịd e-enyʌññọ esio enịm asaña-asaña enọ eti etob Abasi, <verse eid="ROM 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 1:2" />eti etob a-anye amaakenwọnwọñọ ke esed ato mme prọfed e-ekewette ke Adisana Ñwed Abasi, <verse eid="ROM 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 1:3" />ke abaña Ayịn amọ, u-uduod amọ nte awo aketooho ubon Defid, <verse eid="ROM 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 1:4" />ndin ato ke Sịbidịd a-asañake ye adudu, ewọt ke anye ado Ayịn Abasi ke adised ke ñkpa amọ: Yisọs Krais Abọọñ ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 1:5" />Ato ke ntak Ayịn amọ ñnyịn imaibọ mfọn adido mme abọsịd ñnyʌñ ñkoot afịd mme Gentile ite edikop uyio a-atooho ke mbuọdidem ke ntak anyịñ Yisọs. <verse eid="ROM 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 1:6" />Ndin ndufo ñko eba ke atu mme Gentile e-ekoodo nọ edido ake Yisọs Krais.<verse eid="ROM 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 1:7" />Enọ ñwed ami esọk afịd mbon e-ebaaha ke Rom a-Abasi amaaha anyʌñ akoot nọ edido mme ndisana awo amọ: Mfọn ye emem a-atooho Abasi Ete ye Abọọñ Yisọs Krais akpaakap isịm ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 1:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Udọñ Pọọl Adika Rom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 1:8" />Ke akpa ifed, ami mmekọọm Abasi mmi, ke Yisọs Krais, mbaña afịd ndufo naña mbuọdidem ndufo awuọ etob ke afịd ederimbod. <verse eid="ROM 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 1:9" />Abasi, a-ami ñkponoke ke afịd esịd ke adikwọrọ eti etob Ayịn amọ ado ntiense mmi ke naña ami itoiyo ndufo <verse eid="ROM 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 1:10" />afịd ini a-ami mbọññọ akam; ami ñnyʌñ mbọñ akam mbo ke akpatre, ke uduak Abasi, usʌñ akpekap abeere annọ miin nọ ndisoobo ye ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 1:11" />Ami mmenie udọñ adikịt ndufo nọ ami inọ ndufo mme enọ sịbidịd a-adiinọ ndufo nsọñidem, <verse eid="ROM 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 1:12" />nọ ato do ndufo ye ami inọ emọ-emọ nsọọñọnda ato ke mbuọdidem. <verse eid="ROM 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 1:13" />Mme nditọeka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek, ikọ ami, adelfọi, a-awuọñọke </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ideen ye ibaan</char><char style="ft" closed="false">amaana ada anọ mbon e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, ideen ye ibaan, ke atu ubon Abasi; se ñko ke Rom 7:1, 4; Rom 8:12, 29; Rom 10:1; Rom 11:25; Rom 12:1; Rom 15:14, 30; Rom 16:14, 17</char></note> ke Krais, ami ñyemme ndufo etre adidiọọñọ ke ami mmaanam akikere uwak ini adidise ndufo (ado emaeñkpan adinam ntoro tutu idahami) nọ ato do ami nnie utịb ke ufọọd ndufo kpa naña ñkenie ye mme Gentile mfen.<verse eid="ROM 1:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 1:14" />Ami mmenie akpan iso utom adinam nnọọ mbon Greek ye mbon i-imiidooho Greek, ukem ye mbon e-enieghe aniọñ ye mme akọi. <verse eid="ROM 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 1:15" />Ntak ado anam nọ ami nnie akpọsọñ udọñ adikwọrọ eti etob ñko inọọ ndufo e-ebaaha ke Rom.<verse eid="ROM 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 1:16" />Ami ñkoppo abuud ke ntak eti etob, sia anye ado adudu Abasi a-adatta adinyaaña asọk afịd awo e-enịmme ke akpanikọ: Akpa, ado anọ mme Yuu, ndin mme Gentile. <verse eid="ROM 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 1:17" />Sia ke eti etob ke eyaara adinenido a-atooho Abasi, adinen uwem a-atooho ke mbuọdidem tọọñọ ke akpa tutu awuọ akpatre, kpa naña ewet: “Mme ndinen awo ediidu uwem ke mbuọdidem.”<verse eid="ROM 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Abasi Ayat Esịd Abaña Ndiọiñkpọ Uduudawo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 1:18" />E-eyaara iyadesịd Abasi eto hefịn ebaña unana adinie ukpono nnọọ Abasi ye mme ndiọi ido mme awo e-efiighe akpanikọ enịm ato ke ibak ndiọiñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 1:19" />Sia ñkpọ e-ekemeke idiọọñọ mbaña Abasi ana inwañ-inwañ, ke ntak a-adooho Abasi a-anam anye ana inwañ-inwañ anọ ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 1:20" />Sia tọọñọ ke ntọọñọ ederimbod, edu Abasi a-awo imiikịtte, nsi-nsi adudu ye ndisana uduud amọ, ekiit ammọ mfọn-mfọn, ato ke se emaekenam, nọ ato do mme awo edinie ntak aditre adidiọọñọ anye.<verse eid="ROM 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 1:21" />Sia akpesʌkado ammọ emaekediọọñọ Abasi, ammọ ikinọọhọ anye ubọọñ nte Abasi inyʌññọ inọ anye ekọọm, ado akikere ammọ amaakappa ado ikpu-ikpu, ndisịme esịd ammọ ñko emaekịm. <verse eid="ROM 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 1:22" />Akpesʌkado a-ammọ ekereke ke mmimọ ido mme adiọọñọñkpọ, ammọ emaekappa edoñño ndisịme, <verse eid="ROM 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 1:23" />enyʌñ ekpəho ubọọñ Abasi i-imiikemeke adikpa tutu amama esịn ke mme ubobodñkpọ, ke uduud awo, ke mbid inuen ye unam ye se inyọnyọọn ke idịb.<verse eid="ROM 1:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 1:24" />Ke ntak ado Abasi amaayaak ammọ ke ndiọi udọñ esịd ammọ anọ mbubiam ido ke adisuakka idem ammọ ye emọ-emọ. <verse eid="ROM 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 1:25" />Ammọ emaekpəhọ akpanikọ Abasi enọ nsu, ekpono enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ se ebobot ke ubọk utu ke Andibod a-anaaha etooro ke nsi-nsi. Amen.<verse eid="ROM 1:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 1:26" />Ke ntak ami, Abasi amaayaak ammọ anọ mme ndiọi udọñ itọñ. Ibaan ammọ emaekpuuño ataa uduud e-ekebotto ammọ enọ, ekappa se awo imiikibotto ammọ inọ. <verse eid="ROM 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 1:27" />Ke ukem usʌñ ado, ideen emaenyʌñ ekpọñ nnekke-nnekke usʌñ unie ewuana ye ibaan etịmme edumakka idem ammọ ñkpa-ñkpa. Ideen emaekappa enie ewuana ye ideen ke ndedeghe usʌñ enyʌñ ebọi utịb mbubiam ido ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 1:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 1:28" />Sia ammọ imiikikereke ke a-afọn adinie ifiọk Abasi, Abasi amaayaak ammọ anọ idiọọk iwuod, ndin ammọ enañña se imiikpinaaha enam. <verse eid="ROM 1:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 1:29" />Ammọ ediyọhọ ye afịd nsio-nsio ibak, ndiọi ido, idiọọk itọñ, ye adikpọñ nti usʌñ. Ñko ammọ eyọhọ ye ufịb, uwodawo, ndutịn, abiaña ye ubi. Ammọ ebaaña awo ke edem, <verse eid="ROM 1:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ROM 1:30" />ebiat awo ke ikọ inua, esua Abasi, esọñ anyen, ekịt idem, enyʌñ ewọk inua. Ammọ etʌppọ ntʌppọ usʌñ adinam nsio-nsio ndiọiñkpọ, enyʌñ esọñ iwuod ye ete ye eka ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 1:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ROM 1:31" />Ammọ edoñño ndisịme, enana mbuọdidem, enana ima, enyʌñ enana esịd mbọm. <verse eid="ROM 1:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ROM 1:32" />Akpesʌkado ammọ emaediọọñọ nnen-nnen mbed Abasi, a-abooho ke mme andinam utọ ñkpọ ami e-edot ñkpa, ammọ esʌk ekaka iso enañña mme ñkpọ ami enyʌñ edaara mbon se inañña mme utọ ido ami.<verse eid="ROM 1:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="ROM 2" />
  <para style="s1">Adinen Ubiireikpe Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 2:1" />Ndin afo, a-akpeeghe ikpe anọọ awo mfen, unieghe ntak, sia naña afo akpe ikpe mbon mfen, afo ñko abiom idem mfo ikpe, sia afo akpeikpe anam ukem mme ñkpọ ado. <verse eid="ROM 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 2:2" />Ndin ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke ubiireikpe Abasi a-abañake mbon e-enamma utọ ñkpọ ami akọñọ ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ROM 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 2:3" />Ndin afo ñkaña awo, umaubiire ikpe unọ ammọ ado afo asʌk anam ukem ñkpọ ado, afo akere abo ke imọ iyaibọkkọ ubiomikpe Abasi? <verse eid="ROM 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 2:4" />Me afo asịn uwak mfọnido Abasi, ediyọ ye ime amọ ke ndek? Ado nte afo udiọọñọke ke mfọnido Abasi ado adinam afo atua ñkpọfiọk?<verse eid="ROM 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 2:5" />Ado ke ntak nsọñiwuod ye unana adikappa esịd, afo asʌk akọ ifiobesịd anịm anọ idem mfo ke usen iyadesịd Abasi, ke ini adinen ubiireikpe amọ adiiyaara. <verse eid="ROM 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 2:6" />Abasi “ayaanọ awo keedekeed utịb akeene se ammọ enam.” <verse eid="ROM 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 2:7" />Amaado mbon e-esịnne ifịk ke adinam nti ñkpọ, eyem ubọọñ, ukpono ye unana ñkpa nsi-nsi, anye ayaanọ nsi-nsi uwem. <verse eid="ROM 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 2:8" />Ado amaado mbon e-eyemme ubọọñ idem ammọ, enyʌñ esịn akpanikọ, ndin ekeene idiọọk, ifiobesịd ye iyadesịd Abasi ayaaba. <verse eid="ROM 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 2:9" />Afanekọñ ye nnananyen ayaaba anọ afịd awo e-enamma idiọọk, akpa, anọ mme Yuu, ndin mme Gentile. <verse eid="ROM 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 2:10" />Ado ubọọñ, ukpono ye emem anie afịd awo se inam nti ñkpọ; akpa anọ mme Yuu, ndin mme Gentile. <verse eid="ROM 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 2:11" />Sia Abasi akpe ikpe afịd awo ukem-ukem.<verse eid="ROM 2:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 2:12" />Afịd awo se inam idiọọk ke unana mbed eyaekịt nsobo ke unana mbed, ndin afịd awo se inam idiọọkñkpọ ke idak mbed eyaebọ ubiireikpe ke idak mbed. <verse eid="ROM 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 2:13" />Sia idooho mbon se ikop mbed edoñño ndinen ke iso Abasi, ado mbon se inam mbed ke ediikoot ndinen. <verse eid="ROM 2:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 2:14" />(Ke akpanikọ, ke ini mme Gentile i-imiinieghe mbed, enamma ke uduud ammọ nte awo mme ñkpọ e-ekewette ke mbed, ammọ edo mbed enọ idem ammọ, akpọkọm a-ammọ imiinieghe mbed. <verse eid="ROM 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 2:15" />Sia ammọ e-ewọt ke se mbed ayem awere ke esịd ammọ. Akikere esịd ammọ ado ntiense, ndin akikere ado abiom ammọ ikpe usʌk ini, anyʌñ afak ammọ asio ñko usʌk ini.) <verse eid="ROM 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 2:16" />Ami ayaadat itie ke usen a-Abasi adiikpe ikpe ibaña mme ndịbe ñkpọ uduud awo ato ke Yisọs Krais naña eti etob mmi atañ.<verse eid="ROM 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Yuu ye Mbed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 2:17" />Idahami afo, adieke afo akoodo idem mfo Yuu, akpedo ada ke mbed ndin anam inua abaña ewuana mfo ye Abasi, <verse eid="ROM 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 2:18" />akpedo afo amediọọñọ uduak amọ anyʌñ anyịmme se ifọn ikan ke ntak a-adooho afo amediọọñọ mbed; <verse eid="ROM 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 2:19" />akpedo afo amenịm ke afo ado adadusʌñ anọ mme nnan, ado unwana anọ mme andiba ke ekịm, <verse eid="ROM 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 2:20" />ado anọitem anọ mme akọi, ado andikpeeb anọ ntəkayịn, sia afo amenie ke mbed ayọhọ ifiọk ye akpanikọ; <verse eid="ROM 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 2:21" />afo ndin, a-akpeebe mbon mfen, ukpeebe idem mfo ñko? Afo a-akwọrọke abo awo akuuyịp inọ, nte afo ameyịp inọ? <verse eid="ROM 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 2:22" />Afo a-abooho mme awo ekuusịn efịbe, nte afo amesịn efịbe? Afo a-asuaha usọsọiñkpọ, afo ameyiip ñkpọ ke mme tembịd? <verse eid="ROM 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 2:23" />Afo a-awọkkọ inua abaña mbed, nte afo ametre ikpono Abasi ke adibiat mbed? <verse eid="ROM 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 2:24" />Nte naña ewet: “E-esịn anyịñ Abasi ke ndek ke atu mme Gentile ato ke ntak mfo.”<verse eid="ROM 2:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 2:25" />Adifọọrọ edʌd a-afọn akpedo afo amenịm mbed, ado akpedo amebiat mbed, amekappa aba nte awo ikuufọọrọke fiin edʌd. <verse eid="ROM 2:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 2:26" />Ke ntoro, adieke mbio i-imiifọọrọke edʌd enamma se isịne ke mbed, nte awo idiidatta ammọ nte mme afọọrọ edʌd? <verse eid="ROM 2:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 2:27" />Awo i-imiifọọrọke edʌd ke abʌkidem, ado anam se mbed atemme, ayaubiom fiin ikpe, sia afo ado abiad mbed, akpesʌkado a-afo anieghe uwewed mbed anyʌññọ afọọrọ edʌd.<verse eid="ROM 2:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 2:28" />Awo idooho Yuu ke abʌkidem ikpọọñ, kpa naña adifọọrọ edʌd miidooho se ekịt ke anyen me ke abʌkidem ikpọọñ. <verse eid="ROM 2:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 2:29" />Iyoo, awo ado Yuu ke esịd idem; ndin ufọọrọ edʌd, ado ufọọrọ edʌd ake esịd, ke Sịbidịd, idooho ke uwewed mbed. Utọ itooro ado itooho awo, ado ato Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 2:29" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="ROM 3" />
  <para style="s1">Anam Akpanikọ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 3:1" />Nsoo ndin ido udod a-abaaha ke adido Yuu, nsoo inyʌñ ido ufọn a-asịneke ke adifọọrọ edʌd? <verse eid="ROM 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 3:2" />A-afọn ke afịd usʌñ! Ke akpa ifed, eyaak ikọ Abasi esịn mme Yuu ke ubọk.<verse eid="ROM 3:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 3:3" />Yak ise ise, akpedo usʌk ammọ inịmme ke akpanikọ-ọ? Nte unana ammọ adinam akpanikọ ayaabiat akpanikọ Abasi? <verse eid="ROM 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 3:4" />Iyoo! Yak Abasi asʌk ado anam akpanikọ, akpekọm afịd awo edoñño mme asʌhọ nsu. Kpa naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 3:4">“Nọ ato do ewọt ke afo amenen ke se afo atañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 3:4">anyʌñ anie edikan ke ini afo akpeeghe ikpe.”<verse eid="ROM 3:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 3:5" />Ado adieke mme ukwañ ido ñnyịn asioho adinenido Abasi adaaha anwa-anwa, nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiitañ? Nte Abasi inenne ke adiben ifiobesịd amọ idot ñnyịn? (Ami ñkama eniin ifiọk awo ntañ ikọ.) <verse eid="ROM 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 3:6" />Idooho ntoro! Akpedo ado ntoro, Abasi akpenam die akpe ikpe ederimbod? <verse eid="ROM 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 3:7" />Awo akeme adifaaña mbo, “Adieke nsu-nsu uwem mmi anamma akpanikọ Abasi awuọ anyʌñ anam ubọọñ amọ akpon, nsoo ido ntak e-embiommo miin ikpe nte anam idiọọkñkpọ?” <verse eid="ROM 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 3:8" />Ntak a-awo imiitañña naña usʌk awo ebo ke ñnyịn ibo “Yak ñnyịn inam idiọọkñkpọ nọ nti ñkpọ awuọ adi-e?” Ubiomikpe ammọ adot.<verse eid="ROM 3:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adinen Awo Ibaaha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 3:9" />Nsoo ido utịd iwuod ikọ ñnyịn ndin? Nte ñnyịn imifọn ikan ammọ? Idooho ntoro! Ñnyịn imiwọwọt ibo ke mme Yuu ukem-ukem ye mme Gentile eba ke idak idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="ROM 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 3:10" />Nte naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 3:10">“Ibaaha awo se inen, ibaaha awo ndomokeed;<verse eid="ROM 3:10" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 3:11" />ibaaha awo keed se ñkpọ anwaña;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 3:11">ibaaha awo ndomokeed a-ayemme Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 3:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 3:12" />Afịd ammọ e-ekpọñ usʌñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 3:12">afịd ediana keed ekappa mme ñkpafi;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 3:12">ibaaha awo keed a-anamma eti,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 3:12">ibaaha awo ndomokeed.”<verse eid="ROM 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 3:13" />“Usʌñ itọñ ammọ edoñño mme anainwañ udi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 3:13">edeme ammọ enam abiaña.”</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 3:13">“Idiọọk ifod udʌkikọd ayọhọ ñkpọkinua ammọ.”<verse eid="ROM 3:13" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 3:14" />“Mme inua ammọ eyọhọ ye nsueñ ye idiọọkesịd.”<verse eid="ROM 3:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 3:15" />“Ñkpad ammọ esọp ke uduọk iyiib;<verse eid="ROM 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 3:16" />atahade ye ukuud eyọhọ usʌñ ammọ,<verse eid="ROM 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 3:17" />ndin usʌñ emem, ammọ idiọọñọke,”<verse eid="ROM 3:17" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 3:18" />“Mbaak Abasi ibaaha ammọ ke idem.”<verse eid="ROM 3:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 3:19" />Idahami ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke se adodo a-mbed atañña, atañ anọ mbon e-ebaaha ke idak mbed, nọ afịd ederimbod edisịne ke ubiireikpe Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 3:20" />Ke ntak ado awo ndomokeed idooho adinen ke iso Abasi ke adinịm mbed; utu ke ado, ato ke mbed ñnyịn idiọọñọ idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="ROM 3:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adinenido Ato Mbuọdidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 3:21" />Ado idahami e-enam ediọọñọ adinenido a-atooho Abasi, ke esioho mbed efep: Mbed ye mme Prọfed edoñño mme ntiense. <verse eid="ROM 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 3:22" />Adinenido ato Abasi ke mbuọdidem ke Yisọs Krais anọ afịd mbon se inịm ke akpanikọ. Ukpʌhọ ndomokeed ibaaha ke ufọọd mme Yuu ye mme Gentile, <verse eid="ROM 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 3:23" />sia afịd awo e-enam idiọọkñkpọ enyʌñ ewuọ ekpọñ ubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 3:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 3:24" />Afịd awo enyʌñ e-ekịt unen ke mfọn a-atooho adifak ake Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="ROM 3:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 3:25" />Abasi amaanọ Krais nte uwa a-akpeeghe isob asio awo ke idiọọkñkpọ ato ke iyiib amọ a-anaaha ebọ eto mbuọdidem. Anye akenam ami adiwọt ido amọ sia ke adiyọ ammọ anye amaafeen mme idiọọkñkpọ e-ekenamma ke usen edem, inyʌññọ imia ammọ ufen. <verse eid="ROM 3:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 3:26" />Abasi akenam ami adiwọt adinenido amọ ke ayio ami, nọ anye anen anyʌñ ado andinam mbon e-enịmme Yisọs ke akpanikọ enen.<verse eid="ROM 3:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 3:27" />Ñwọkinua ñnyịn ndin asịne ke nsoo? E-esio anye ado efep. Ke ntak mbed akee? Me ke mbed asañake ye utom? Iyoo, ado ke ntak mbed ayemme mbuọdidem. <verse eid="ROM 3:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 3:28" />Sia ñnyịn isʌk ibo ke awo anen ato ke mbuọdidem, ke aboiyoke adinam se mbed abo enam. <verse eid="ROM 3:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 3:29" />Me nte Abasi ado Abasi mme Yuu ikpọọñ? Nte anye idooho Abasi mme Gentile ñko? Ii, ake mme Gentile ñko, <verse eid="ROM 3:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ROM 3:30" />sia ado Abasi keed kpọd aba, a-adiinọ mbon e-efọọrọke edʌd ke mbuọdidem unen ye mbio imiifọọrọke edʌd kpa ke ntak mbuọdidem keed ado. <verse eid="ROM 3:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ROM 3:31" />Nte ñnyịn ndin imibiat mbed ke ntak mbuọdidem ami? Idooho ntoro! Utu ke ado, ñnyịn isọọsọọñọ mbed.<verse eid="ROM 3:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="ROM 4" />
  <para style="s1">Ebraham Akenen Ato Mbuọdidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 4:1" />Nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiibo, ke Ebraham, akpa ete ñnyịn ke ikpọkidem, akeyaara abaña ñkpọ ami? <verse eid="ROM 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 4:2" />Akpedo, ke akpanikọ, ekenam Ebraham anen ye Abasi ato utom amọ, anye amaanie ñkpọ se anye akpedat awọk inua, ado idooho ke iso Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 4:3" />Nsoo ke ikọ Abasi atañ? “Ebraham amaanịm Abasi ke akpanikọ, ndin emaebat enọ anye nte adinenido.”<verse eid="ROM 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 4:4" />Ke aditʌm ntañ, awo amaanam utom, awo ibatta akʌkutom amọ inọ anye nte enọ, ado edat nte unen amọ. <verse eid="ROM 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 4:5" />Ñko, awo a-mmiinamma utom, ado anịm Abasi a-atoppoke mme andidue ikpe ke akpanikọ, ebat mbuọdidem ammọ nte adinenido. <verse eid="ROM 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 4:6" />Ukem-ukem ami ke Defid abo idaha a-anye atañña abaña adidiọñ awo a-Abasi adatta nte adinenido ke esioho mme utom efep:<verse eid="ROM 4:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 4:7" />“Afọfọn anọ mbon</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 4:7">e-efeene mme ukwañido ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 4:7">e-enyʌññọ efʌk mme ndiọiñkpọ ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 4:8" />Afọfọn anọ awo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 4:8">a-Abọọñ imiidibatta idiọọkñkpọ amọ inọ anye.”<verse eid="ROM 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 4:9" />Nte adidiọñ ami ana anọ mbon e-efọọrọke edʌd ikpọọñ, me ana anọ mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd ñko? Ñnyịn isʌk ibo ke emaebat mbuọdidem Ebraham enọ anye nte adinenido. <verse eid="ROM 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 4:10" />Ke nsoo ntak ke ekebat enọ anye? Me ke emaekefọọrọ anye edʌd me mbemiso ekefọọrọ anye edʌd? Ikidooho ke emaekefọọrọ anye edʌd; akedo mbemiso! <verse eid="ROM 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 4:11" />Anye akebọ ufọọrọ edʌd nte idiọọñọ ye adisọọñọ adinenido a-anye amaakenenie ke mbuọdidem ke ini awo imiikifọọrọke anye edʌd. Ke ntak ado, anye ñko ado ete afịd mme andinịm ke akpanikọ, akpesʌkado a-awo imiikifọọrọke ammọ edʌd nọ ato do ebat adinenido enọ ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 4:12" />Ndin anye ñko anyʌñ ado ete mbon e-emaekefọọrọ edʌd; idooho ado ikpọọñ, ado ado ete ñko anọ mbon e-esañake ke ñkpad isañ mme andinie mbuọdidem e-ete ñnyịn Ebraham akenieghe mbemiso ekefọọrọ anye edʌd.<verse eid="ROM 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 4:13" />Ikitooho ke mbed ke Ebraham ye mme nditọ amọ ekebọọ ikọ enwọñọ ete ke anye adiido adiaakpa ederimbod, ado ato adinenido a-asañake ke mbuọdidem. <verse eid="ROM 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 4:14" />Sia adieke mbon e-edotto anyen ke mbed edoññoke mme adiaakpa, mbuọdidem inieghe ufọn, ado ikpu-ikpu, ñko enwọñọ iwuọñọke ñkpọ. <verse eid="ROM 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 4:15" />Sia mbed adat ifiobesịd adi. Ndin, itie nte mbed imiibaaha ubiad mbed ñko ibaaha.<verse eid="ROM 4:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 4:16" />Ke ntak ami, enwọñọ asaña ye mbuọdidem nọ ato ke mfọn anyʌñ ana anọ nditọ Ebraham, inaaha inọ mbon e-enịmme mbed ikpọọñ, ado ana ñko anọ mbon e-enieghe mbuọdidem Ebraham. Sia Ebraham ado ete afịd ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 4:17" />Kpa naña ewet: “Ami mmenam afo ado ete uwak mme idịd.” Anye ado ete ñnyịn ke iso Abasi, a-anye akenịmme ke akpanikọ, Abasi a-anọọhọ mme akpañkpa uwem anyʌñ akoot asịn ke uwem mme ñkpọ i-imiikibaaha.<verse eid="ROM 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 4:18" />Ke ini idodanyen imiikibaaha, Ebraham ke idodanyen amaanịm anyʌñ akappa ado ete uwak mme idịd, kpa naña emaeketañ enọ anye ebo, “Ntoro ke ubon mfo adiiba.” <verse eid="ROM 4:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 4:19" />Ke unana adinam mbuọdidem amọ amem, amaanwaña Ebraham nte ke ikpọkidem amọ akeba nte ikpọkidem amaakekpa, sia anye akedo ñkpọ nte awo isua ikie, ndin idịb Sera amaanyʌñ akpa. <verse eid="ROM 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 4:20" />Kpayeado anye ikiyịkke enwọñọ Abasi ito ke unana adinịm ke akpanikọ, ado amaasọọñọ ada ke mbuọdidem amọ anyʌñ anọ Abasi ubọọñ. <verse eid="ROM 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 4:21" />Anye amaanekke anịm ke esịd amọ ate ke Abasi a-anie adudu adinam se anye akenwọñọ. <verse eid="ROM 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 4:22" />Ami ado ntak “ekebatta enọ anye nte adinenido.” <verse eid="ROM 4:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 4:23" />Mme ikọ e-ebooho, “ekebatta enọ anye” idooho anye ikpọọñ ke ekewet enọ, <verse eid="ROM 4:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 4:24" />ado ñnyịn ñko, a-Abasi adiibat adinenido inọ, ñnyịn i-inịmme ke akpanikọ ke anye akenam Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs aset ke ñkpa. <verse eid="ROM 4:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 4:25" />Ekeyaak anye enọ ñkpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ñnyịn enyʌñ enam anye aset ke ñkpa adʌk uwem ke adinam ñnyịn inen ye Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 4:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="ROM 5" />
  <para style="s1">Emem ye Idodanyen</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 5:1" />Do ndin, sia emaekenam ñnyịn inen ato ke mbuọdidem, ñnyịn iminie emem ye Abasi ato ke Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais. <verse eid="ROM 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 5:2" />Ato ke anye ñnyịn imidʌk ke mbuọdidem, inie mfọn a-ñnyịn isọọñọke ida idahami. Ndin ñnyịn iminam inua ke idodanyen ke ubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 5:3" />Idooho ado ikpọọñ, ado ñnyịn ñko imikop idadesịd ke ukuud ñnyịn, sia ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke ukuud aben ime adi. <verse eid="ROM 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 5:4" />Ime anọ eti uduud, ndin eti uduud anọ idodanyen. <verse eid="ROM 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 5:5" />Ñko idodanyen isịnne ñnyịn ke abuud, sia Abasi a-anwañña ima amọ asịn ke esịd ñnyịn, ato ke Adisana Sịbidịd a-anye inọọhọ ñnyịn.<verse eid="ROM 5:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 5:6" />Ndufo emekịt ke adikem ini, ke ini ñnyịn imiikinieghe inweek, Krais amaakpa anọ mbon i-imiidiọọñọke Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 5:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 5:7" />A-asọñ eti-eti awo adikpa nnọọ adinen awo, ñkọm a-adooho ke iwuod eti awo, awo akeme idomo adikpa. <verse eid="ROM 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 5:8" />Ado Abasi i-iwọt ñnyịn ima amọ sia naña ñnyịn ikisʌkkọ ido mme anam idiọọkñkpọ, Krais amaakpa inọ ñnyịn.<verse eid="ROM 5:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 5:9" />Sia emaekinam ñnyịn inie unen ato ke iyiib amọ, anye ñko ayainyaaña ñnyịn asio ke ifiobesịd Abasi! <verse eid="ROM 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 5:10" />Sia adieke adooho ke ini ñnyịn ikikappa ido asua ye Abasi, ekenam emem ke ufọọd ñnyịn ye Abasi ato ke ntak ñkpa Ayịn amọ, kap se idahami ndin a-ñnyịn idooho keed ye anye, adinyaaña ñnyịn adiikpon die ito uwem amọ! <verse eid="ROM 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 5:11" />Ikweeñeke ke ado, ñnyịn iduaak inua ke Abasi ato Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais, a-anamma ñnyịn inie ewuana ye Abasi idahami.<verse eid="ROM 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkpa Ato Adam, Uwem Ato Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 5:12" />Ke ntoro, kpa naña idiọọkñkpọ aketo awo keed adʌk ederimbod, ñkpa anyʌñ ato idiọọkñkpọ, ke utọ usʌñ ami ñkpa amaasịm afịd awo, sia afịd awo emaenam idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="ROM 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 5:13" />Ke adinekke ntañ, idiọọkñkpọ amaababa ke ederimbod, mbemiso enọ mbed, ado awo ibatta idiọọkñkpọ inọ awo ke ini mbed imiibaaha. <verse eid="ROM 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 5:14" />Kpayeado, ñkpa amaakara tọọñọ ke ayio Adam tutu asịm ini Moses, anyʌñ adoro kpa mbon i-ikidiinamma idiọọkñkpọ ke adibiat mbed, naña Adam akenam, a-akedooho uwọdñkpọ awo a-adiidi.<verse eid="ROM 5:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 5:15" />Ado enọ ami ibaaha nte adinam idiọọkñkpọ. Sia adieke uwak awo ekekpaññake eto ke awo keed adibiat ewʌhọ, adaña die ke mfọn Abasi ye enọ a-akesañake ye mfọn awo keed, a-adooho Yisọs Krais, akpefiọrọ asịm uwak awo! <verse eid="ROM 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 5:16" />Mfen, awo ikemeke iben enọ Abasi ndomo ye utịb idiọọkñkpọ awo keed: Ubiireikpe akekeene idiọọkñkpọ keed ndin adat ubiomikpe adi, ado enọ ado akekeene mme uwak ndudue anyʌñ adat unen adi. <verse eid="ROM 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 5:17" />Sia adieke atooho ke idiọọkñkpọ awo keed, ñkpa akara ato ke awo keed, die ndin ke afịd mbon se ibọ uwak mfọn Abasi ye enọ adinenido ediikara ke uwem ito awo keed ado, kpa Yisọs Krais.<verse eid="ROM 5:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 5:18" />Ke ntoro, sia aketooho idiọọkñkpọ awo keed, ubiomikpe asịm afịd awo, ukem ado ñko ke utịb adinam etiido keed akedat utoppo ikpe ye uwem asọk afịd awo. <verse eid="ROM 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 5:19" />Sia aketooho ke ntịdutọñ awo keed emaenam uwak awo edo mme anam ndiọiñkpọ, ntoro ñko ato ke nsuukiwuod awo keed, eyaenam uwak awo enen.<verse eid="ROM 5:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 5:20" />Ekedat mbed edi nọ ndudue atọt. Ado naña idiọọkñkpọ atọt, ntoro ke mfọn adọdiọñ atọt, <verse eid="ROM 5:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 5:21" />nọ ato do, kpa naña idiọọkñkpọ akekara ke ñkpa, mfọn ñko akpekara ato adinenido a-adiidat nsi-nsi uwem a-atooho Yisọs Krais Abọọñ ñnyịn idi.<verse eid="ROM 5:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="ROM 6" />
  <para style="s1">Adikpa Ñwuọ ke Idiọọkñkpọ, Nnie Uwem ke Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 6:1" />Nsoo ke ñnyịn idiitañ, ndin? Nte ana ñnyịn ika iso inam idiọọkñkpọ nọ ato do mfọn atọt? <verse eid="ROM 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 6:2" />Nwaaña nsa-o! Die ke ñnyịn i-imaikikpañña inọ idiọọkñkpọ idiika iso inyịne ke idiọọkñkpọ ado? <verse eid="ROM 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 6:3" />Nte ñnyịn idiọọñọke ke afịd ñnyịn i-imaikibọ uduọkmmọọñ ke Krais Yisọs imaibọ uduọkmmọọñ ñko idʌk ke ñkpa amọ? <verse eid="ROM 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 6:4" />Emaibuuk ñnyịn ñko ye anye ato uduọkmmọọñ ke ñkpa nọ ato do, naña ekenam Krais aset ke ñkpa ato ke ubọọñ Ete amọ, ñnyịn ñko idiinyʌñ idu ufa uwem.<verse eid="ROM 6:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 6:5" />Sia akpedo ñnyịn imidiana ye anye ke ukem ñkpa amọ, ñnyịn ñko idiitreke adidiana ye anye ke ukem adised ke ñkpa amọ. <verse eid="ROM 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 6:6" />Sia ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke emaekọñ akaan uduud ñnyịn ke krọs ye anye nọ idiọọkñkpọ abʌkidem aboiyo afep, mbaak ñnyịn idika iso isịne ke ufʌn idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="ROM 6:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 6:7" />Sia awo keed akeedodo a-amaakekpa, abọkkọ idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="ROM 6:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 6:8" />Do ndin adieke ñnyịn ikikpaaha ye Krais, ñnyịn iminịm ke ñnyịn ñko iyaidu uwem ye anye. <verse eid="ROM 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 6:9" />Sia ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke emaenam Krais aset ke ñkpa, anye ikemeke adikpa aba; ñkpa inieghe adudu ke idem amọ aba. <verse eid="ROM 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 6:10" />Ñkpa a-anye akekpaaha, anye akekpa akañ keed anọ idiọọkñkpọ afịd awo; ado uwem a-anye aduuho, anye adu anọ Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 6:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 6:11" />Kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, ibat idem ndufo nte ke emaekpa enọ idiọọkñkpọ, ado edu uwem enọ Abasi ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="ROM 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 6:12" />Ndin ikiiyak idiọọkñkpọ akara ikpọkidem ndufo mbaak ndufo idinam ndiọi udọñ amọ. <verse eid="ROM 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 6:13" />Ikiiyaak itie ndomokeed ke idem ndufo inọọ idiọọkñkpọ, nte ñkpọutom ibak. Utu ke ado iyaak idem ndufo inọ Abasi, nte mbon e-emaekesio ke ñkpa esịn ke uwem. Ke ntoro iyaak afịd idem ndufo inọ anye nte ñkpọutom adinenido. <verse eid="ROM 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 6:14" />Ndin idiọọkñkpọ idiidooho eteufọk ndufo aba, sia ndufo ibaaha ke idak mbed, ado eba ke idak mfọn.<verse eid="ROM 6:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Udʌk Ufʌn Nnọọ Adinenido</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 6:15" />Nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiinam? Ana nte ñnyịn inam idiọọkñkpọ sia ñnyịn imiibaaha ke idak mbed ado iba ke idak mfọn? Nwaaña nsa-o! <verse eid="ROM 6:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 6:16" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke imaiyaak idem ndufo inọ awo nte ifʌn, ndufo edo ifʌn enọ awo a-ndufo ekoppo uyio amọ, me ndufo edo ifʌn enọ idiọọkñkpọ, a-adatta aka ñkpa, me ñkobuyio, a-adatta aka adinenido? <verse eid="ROM 6:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 6:17" />Ado mmekọọm Abasi ke akpesʌkado a-ndufo ekesidooho ifʌn enọọ idiọọkñkpọ, ndufo emaenam se ekikpeep ndufo ke afịd esịd ndin anye akappa ado usʌñ ñkobitem ndufo idahami. <verse eid="ROM 6:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 6:18" />Emaifak ndufo esio ke abʌkidem idiọọkñkpọ ndin ndufo emekappa edo ifʌn enọ adinenido.<verse eid="ROM 6:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 6:19" />Ami ntañ ami ñkene naña uwem aba ke usen ke usen, sia ndufo emenie mmemidem abʌkidem nte awo. Kpa naña ndufo ekesịyaak idem ndufo nte ifʌn enọọ mme ndedehe ñkpọ ye akpakʌb uwem ibak, idahami ana ekappa edo ifʌn enọ adinenido a-adatta aka adisana uwem. <verse eid="ROM 6:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 6:20" />Ke ini ndufo ekedooho ifʌn enọọ idiọọkñkpọ, ndufo ikisịneke ke idak ukara adinenido. <verse eid="ROM 6:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 6:21" />Nsoo ufọn ndin ke ndufo ekebọọ ke ini ado eto mme ñkpọ i-imʌmmọ ndufo abuud idahami? Mme ñkpọ ado edat eka ñkpa! <verse eid="ROM 6:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 6:22" />Ado idahami emaisio ndufo ke idiọọkñkpọ, ndufo enyʌñ ekappa edo ifʌn Abasi. Ufọn a-ndufo ediaha eto ado adisana uwem, ndin utịb ado nsi-nsi uwem. <verse eid="ROM 6:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 6:23" />Sia utịb idiọọkñkpọ ado ñkpa, ado enọ Abasi ado nsi-nsi uwem ke Krais Yisọs Abọọñ ñnyịn.<verse eid="ROM 6:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="ROM 7" />
  <para style="s1">Adikpọk Ñyaak ke Mbed ye Adimʌm Ndian ke Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 7:1" />Nditọeka mmi ke Krais, ado nte ndufo idiọọñọke, sia ami ntañ ikọ nnọ mbon e-ediọọñọke mbed, ke mbed akara awo ke ini anye abaaha ke uwem? <verse eid="ROM 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 7:2" />Nte uwọdñkpọ, ke mbed, awonwaan ufọk ndọ adiana ye ebe amọ adaña nte ebe amọ abaaha ke uwem, ado ebe akpekpa, e-etat awonwaan ado esio ke mbed ndọ. <verse eid="ROM 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 7:3" />Ndin, adieke awonwaan ado anieghe ewuana ye awodeen mfen ke ini ebe amọ abaaha ke uwem, ekoot awonwaan ado asịn efịbe. Ado adieke ebe amọ akpaaha, e-etat anye esio ke idak mbed ndọ, ndin anye idooho asịn efịbe aba, akpekọm anye adọ ebe mfen.<verse eid="ROM 7:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 7:4" />Ke ntoro, nditọeka mmi ke Krais, ndufo ñko emaekpañña ewuọọñọ ke mbed ato ke ikpọkidem Krais nọ ato do ndufo enie ewuana ye awo mfen, anye a-akesette ke ñkpa, nọ ñnyịn inwịm mfịd inọ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 7:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 7:5" />Sia ke ini abʌkidem akikarake ñnyịn, mme ndiọi udọñ a-mbed akedemmeke, e-ekebaaha ke utom ke idem ñnyịn, emaenam ñnyịn inwịm mfịd inọ ñkpa. <verse eid="ROM 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 7:6" />Ado idahami, ke adikpa nnọọ ñkpọ se ikimʌm ñnyịn ikama ke usen edem, i-itat ñnyịn esio ke mbed nọ ñnyịn inam utom ke ufa usʌñ Sịbidịd, idooho ke akaan usʌñ uwewed mbed.<verse eid="ROM 7:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mbed ye Idiọọkñkpọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 7:7" />Nsoo ke ñnyịn idiitañ ndin? Nte mbed ado idiọọkñkpọ? Nsa-o! Ado ke akpanikọ, ami ñkpekediọọñọke se idiọọkñkpọ ado ke esioho mbed efep. Sia ami ñkpekediọọñọke se isịnanyen ado adieke mbed imiikpikibooho, “Kuusịn anyen ke ñkpọ awo.” <verse eid="ROM 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 7:8" />Ado idiọọkñkpọ, a-adidatta ifed a-mbed anọọhọ, asioño ke idem mmi mme nsio-nsio udọñ isịnanyen. Sia emaesio mbed efep, idiọọkñkpọ akpa. <verse eid="ROM 7:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 7:9" />Idaha a-mbed imiikibaaha ami mmaadu uwem, ado ewʌhọ akedi, idiọọkñkpọ adakka ada anie uwem, ndin ami ñkpa. <verse eid="ROM 7:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 7:10" />Ami mmaadikịt ke ado ewʌhọ ke idem amọ a-akpedatta uwem adi akappa adat ñkpa adi. <verse eid="ROM 7:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 7:11" />Ndin idiọọkñkpọ a-adatta ufañ e-ewʌhọ anọọhọ, amambiaña miin, ndin ato ke ewʌhọ anye a-ansịn miin ke ñkpa. <verse eid="ROM 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 7:12" />Do ndin mbed asana, ewʌhọ ñko asana, anen anyʌñ afọn.<verse eid="ROM 7:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 7:13" />Nte eti ñkpọ amaakappa ado ñkpa annọ miin? Nwaaña nsa-o! Ado nọ ediọọñọ idiọọkñkpọ nte idiọọkñkpọ, anye a-adat ñkpa ansọk miin ato ke se ikifọn nọ ato ke ewʌhọ idiọọkñkpọ anenekke adiọọk.<verse eid="ROM 7:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 7:14" />Ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke mbed ado sịbidịd; ado ami ndooho sịbidịd, ndo abʌkidem e-emaekenyam nte afʌn enọ idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="ROM 7:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 7:15" />Ami ndiọọñọke se ami nnam. Sia se ami ñyem adinam ami nnamma, ado se ami nsua, kpa ado ke ami nnam. <verse eid="ROM 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 7:16" />Ndin adieke ami nnamma se ami mmeñyemme inam, ami mmenyịmme ke mbed afọn. <verse eid="ROM 7:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 7:17" />Awuọ idooho ami ke idem mmi nnam ñkpọ, ado idiọọkñkpọ a-adʌññọ ke idem mmi anam. <verse eid="ROM 7:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 7:18" />Sia ami mmediọọñọ ke eti ñkpọ ndomokeed idʌññọ ke idem mmi, ado ado ke idiọọk uduud mmi. Sia ami mmenie udọñ adinam se ifọn, ado ñkanna nnam. <verse eid="ROM 7:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 7:19" />Sia ami nnamma eti ñkpọ se ami ñyem inam, ado idiọọkñkpọ a-ami mmiiyemme inam, kpa ado ke ami nnam. <verse eid="ROM 7:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 7:20" />Ndin adieke ami nnamma se ami mmiiyemme inam, idooho ami nnam aba, ado idiọọkñkpọ a-adʌññọ ke idem mmi anam.<verse eid="ROM 7:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 7:21" />Do ndin ami mmekịt ke mbed a-anam utom amọ ke idem mi sia akpesʌkado a-ami ñyemme inam se ifọn, idiọọkñkpọ iyakka nnam. <verse eid="ROM 7:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 7:22" />Sia ke ataa esịd idem mmi ami mmenem esịd ke adinịm mbed Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 7:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 7:23" />Ado ami mmekịt mbed mfen a-anamma utom ke idem mmi, a-anwanake ekọñ ye mbed a-abaaha ke akikere mmi anyʌñ anam ami ndo awo ñkpakọb nnọ mbed idiọọkñkpọ a-anamma utom ke esịd idem mmi. <verse eid="ROM 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 7:24" />Nsoo utọ atịme awo ke ami ndo! Anie idiimfak miin isio ke ubọk abʌkidem ñkpa ami? <verse eid="ROM 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 7:25" />Ekọọm anie Abasi, amfakka miin ato ke Yisọs Krais Abọọñ ñnyịn!</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 7:25">Do ndin, ami ke esịd idem mmi ndo afʌn nnọ mbed Abasi, ado ke idiọọk abod mmi ndo afʌn nnọ mbed idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="ROM 7:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="ROM 8" />
  <para style="s1">Uwem ke Sịbidịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 8:1" />Ke ntoro, ubiomikpe ibaaha inọ mbon e-ebaaha ke Krais Yisọs, <verse eid="ROM 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 8:2" />sia ato ke Krais Yisọs ke mbed a-Sịbidịd a-anọọhọ uwem itat ndufo ayaak ke mbed idiọọkñkpọ ye ñkpa. <verse eid="ROM 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 8:3" />Sia se mbed imiikikanna inam ke ntak a-abʌkidem akebọọhọ anye adudu, Abasi amaanam ke adinọ ukweeñe Ayịn amọ ke mbid idiọọk abʌkidem adido uwa ufeen idiọọkñkpọ. Ndin anye amaabiom idiọọkñkpọ ikpe ke abʌkidem, <verse eid="ROM 8:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 8:4" />nọ ato do udọñ unen mbed aba ayọhọ-ayọhọ ke idem ñnyịn, i-imiiduuho uwem ikeene abʌkidem ado ikeene Sịbidịd.<verse eid="ROM 8:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 8:5" />Mbon e-eduuho uwem naña abʌkidem atemme esịn akikere ammọ ke udọñ abʌkidem; ado mbon eduuho uwem ekeene Sịbidịd esịn esịd ammọ ke udọñ Sịbidịd. <verse eid="ROM 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 8:6" />Akikere a-abʌkidem akarake adat aka ñkpa, ado akikere a-Sịbidịd akarake adat aka uwem ye emem. <verse eid="ROM 8:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 8:7" />Akikere a-abʌkidem akarake ado asua ye Abasi; anye isuuho iwuod inọ mbed Abasi, inyʌññọ ikan inịm mbed. <verse eid="ROM 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 8:8" />Mbon a-abʌkidem akarake ikanna inem Abasi esịd.<verse eid="ROM 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 8:9" />Ado, idooho abʌkidem ikara ndufo, ado Sịbidịd ikara, adieke adooho Sịbidịd Abasi adʌñ ke esịd ndufo. Awo imiinieghe Sịbidịd Krais idooho ake Krais. <verse eid="ROM 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 8:10" />Ado adieke Krais adʌññọ ke idem ndufo, akpesʌkado a-abʌkidem ndufo anaaha akpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ, Sịbidịd a-anọ uwem ato ke adinenido. <verse eid="ROM 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 8:11" />Ndin adieke Sịbidịd Abasi a-akenamma Yisọs aset ke ñkpa adʌññọ ye ndufo, anye a-akenamma Krais aset ke ñkpa ayaanyʌñ anọ abʌkidem ndufo uwem ato ke Sịbidịd amọ a-adʌññọ ke idem ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 8:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 8:12" />Ke ntoro, nditọeka ke Krais, ñnyịn iminie iso utom adinam, ado idooho adidu uwem naña abʌkidem ñnyịn ayem. <verse eid="ROM 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 8:13" />Sia ndufo ikpidu uwem ikeene udọñ abʌkidem, ndufo eyaekpañña, ado ikpidu ikeene Sịbidịd, ndufo eyaewot ndiọiñkpọ abʌkidem enyʌñ edu uwem.<verse eid="ROM 8:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 8:14" />Sia mbon a-Sịbidịd Abasi adatta usʌñ, ammọ ikpọọñ edoñño nditọ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 8:15" />Ndufo ikibọọhọ Sịbidịd a-anamma ndufo edoñño ifʌn a-akpenamma ndufo edu uwem ke ndịk, ado ekebọ Sịbidịd nditọ amanaisọñ. Ndin ato ke anye ke ñnyịn ibọñ ikoot, “<char style="tl">Abba,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8:15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Abba ado </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ete ke usem Aramaik</char></note> Ete.” <verse eid="ROM 8:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 8:16" />Sịbidịd ke idem amọ atie ntiense ye sịbidịd ñnyịn ate ke ñnyịn ido nditọ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 8:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 8:17" />Ndin adieke ñnyịn idooho nditọ, ñnyịn ido mme adiaakpa, adiaakpa ake Abasi ye mme ndiana adiaakpa ye Krais; sia adieke ñnyịn iwuanake ke ufen amọ ke akpanikọ, iyainyʌñ iwuana ke ubọọñ amọ ñko.<verse eid="ROM 8:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ufen Idahami ye Ubọọñ Ini Iso</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 8:18" />Ami ndat nte ke ufen a-ñnyịn ibọọhọ idahami idooho se eben edomo ye ubọọñ e-ediiyaara ke idem ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 8:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 8:19" />Afịd abod asʌk abet ke akpọsọñ udọñ adiyaara nditọ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 8:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 8:20" />Sia emaeyak ederimbod esịn ke idak ndutʌhọ, idooho ke unyịmme amọ, ado ato ke uduak awo a-akesịnne anye, ke idodanyen, <verse eid="ROM 8:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 8:21" />ate ke ederimbod ke idem amọ ayaawuọ ke ñkpakọb ufʌn mbiara anyʌñ adʌk ke ubọkkọ ye itooro nditọ Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 8:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 8:22" />Ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke afịd ederimbod asʌk akuun nte aba ke ubiak uman ayịn tutu asịm idahami. <verse eid="ROM 8:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 8:23" />Idooho abod ikpọọñ, ado ñnyịn ke idem ñnyịn i-inieghe akpa mfịd Sịbidịd, ikookuun ke esịd idem nte ñnyịn ibette Abasi ye akpọsọñ udọñ adidat ñnyịn nsịn ke ubọọñ nte nditọ, a-adooho adinyaaña abʌkidem ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 8:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 8:24" />Sia akedo ke idodanyen ami ke ekinyaaña ñnyịn. Ado idodanyen e-ekịtte ke anyen idooho idodanyen ndomokeed. Anie adot anyen ke se anye amaakenenie? <verse eid="ROM 8:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 8:25" />Ado ñnyịn ikpidot anyen ke se ñnyịn imiinieghe diin, ñnyịn ibet ñkpọ ado ke ime.<verse eid="ROM 8:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 8:26" />Ke ukem usʌñ ado, Sịbidịd inyaaña ñnyịn ke ini mmemidem. Ñnyịn idiọọñọke se ñnyịn ikpibeeñe ke akam, ado Sịbidịd ke idem amọ akama ñkuun atie ubiọñ anam ñkpeubọk inọ ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 8:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 8:27" />Ndin anye a-aduuñọke esịd ñnyịn a-adiọọñọ akikere Sịbidịd, sia Sịbidịd atie ubiọñ anọ nditọ Abasi naña asaña ke uduak Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 8:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 8:28" />Ñko ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ibo ke Abasi anam afịd ñkpọ ke ufọn mbon e-emaaha anye, e-ekoodo ekeene uduak amọ. <verse eid="ROM 8:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 8:29" />Sia mbon a-Abasi amaakebabak adiọọñọ, anye amaabak amek ammọ ke mbid Ayịn amọ, nọ anye akappa ado akpa ayịn ke atu uwak nditọeka. <verse eid="ROM 8:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ROM 8:30" />Ndin mbon a-anye amaakemek, anye amaakoot; mbon se anye akekoot, anye amaanam ammọ enen; mbon se anye akenam enen anye amaanyʌñ anọ ammọ ubọọñ.<verse eid="ROM 8:30" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñnyịn Imikan mme Andikan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ROM 8:31" />Sia ñkpọ abaaha ntom, nsoo ke ñnyịn idiitañ? Adieke Abasi abaaha ye ñnyịn, anie akeme adibiọọñọ ñnyịn? <verse eid="ROM 8:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ROM 8:32" />Anye i-imiikibọọhọ Ayịn amọ isuuk, ado ayaak anye anọ ke ntak ñnyịn, die ndin ke anye ñko ukem ye ayịn amọ adiitre aditat ubọk inọọ ñnyịn afịd ñkpọ? <verse eid="ROM 8:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ROM 8:33" />Anie awo adiiben mbon A-Abasi amaakemek ika ikpe? Ado Abasi ke idem amọ anọ unen utoppo ikpe. <verse eid="ROM 8:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ROM 8:34" />Anie ndin adiibiom ñnyịn ikpe? Awo ndomokeed ibaaha. Krais Yisọs a-akekpaaha, a-akanna ado, a-akesette ke ñkpa adʌk uwem, a-anyʌññọ atie ke ubọk nnasia Abasi anam ñkpeubọk inọọ ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 8:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ROM 8:35" />Anie adiidiañña ñnyịn ikpọñ ima Krais? Nte mfịna, me ukuud, me ukọbọ, me akañ, me unana afọñ, me ñkpọ ndịk, me ñkpọ afai, akeme idiañña ñnyịn ikpọñ ima Krais? <verse eid="ROM 8:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ROM 8:36" />Nte naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 8:36">“Ke ntak mfo ñnyịn ikịt ñkpa afịd usen;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 8:36">edat ñnyịn nte mme edọñ a-anaaha ewot.”<verse eid="ROM 8:36" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ROM 8:37" />Iyoo, ke mme afịd ñkpọ ami ñnyịn ido mme andinekke ñkan ato anye a-akimaaha ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 8:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ROM 8:38" />Sia ami mmenekke nnịm mbo ke ñkpa, me uwem, me mme enyere, me mme dimọn, me idahami, me ini iso, me adudu keed akeedodo, <verse eid="ROM 8:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ROM 8:39" />me unyọọñ, me udem, me ñkpọ ndomokeed ke afịd abod, idiikanna idiañña ñnyịn ikpọñ ima Abasi abaaha ke Krais Yisọs Abọọñ ñnyịn.<verse eid="ROM 8:39" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="ROM 9" />
  <para style="s1">Mbʌññọesịd Pọọl ke Abaña Nditọ Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 9:1" />Ami ntañ akpanikọ ke Krais, nsʌhọke nsu; akikere esịd mmi asọọñọ ntoro ato Adisana Sịbidịd. <verse eid="ROM 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 9:2" />Ami mmenie ekamba mfʌhọ ye ubiak ke esịd mmi. <verse eid="ROM 9:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 9:3" />Sia ami ñkpaama ensueñ miin ke idem mmi enyʌñ eñkpịkke miin esio ekpọñ Krais ke ntak mbon mmi, mbon a-ñnyịn itooho ubon keed, <verse eid="ROM 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 9:4" />ubon Isrel. Ammọ edo mbon edatta nte mme amanaisọñ, ammọ enie adisana ubọọñ, mme edioomo, adibọ mbed, ukpono ke tembịd ye mme enwọñọ. <verse eid="ROM 9:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 9:5" />Ammọ enie mme nsọbom, ndin ato ke ammọ ediọọñọ nte Krais aketo adimana nte awo, a-adooho Abasi andikara afịd ñkpọ. Itooro anie anye ke nsi-nsi! Amen.<verse eid="ROM 9:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adimek ake Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 9:6" />Idooho nte ke enwọñọ Abasi awuọ ikpu-ikpu. Sia idooho afịd awo se ito Isrel edo mbon Isrel. <verse eid="ROM 9:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 9:7" />Inyʌññọ ido sia ammọ edoñño ubon Ebraham, awọt abo ke afịd ammọ edoñño nditọ Ebraham. Ke aditʌm ntañ, ñko nte ñwed Abasi atañña “Adiito ke Aisik ke ubon mfo adiisakka.” <verse eid="ROM 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 9:8" />Ke aditañ ke usʌñ mfen, idooho mme uduud nditọ abʌkidem edoñño nditọ Abasi, ado nditọ enwọñọ ke edat nte asaña-asaña ubon Ebraham. <verse eid="ROM 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 9:9" />Sia naña ekewet enwọñọ ado ado ami: “Ini amaakem ami ñyaatịmme ndi, ndin Sera ayaaman ayịn.”<verse eid="ROM 9:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 9:10" />Idooho ado ikpọọñ, Ribeka akenie nditọ anọ ete keed kpọd, akedooho ete ñnyịn Aisik. <verse eid="ROM 9:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 9:11" />Ado, mbemiso mme amanamba ado ekemana me ekenam eti ñkpọ me idiọọk, nọ uduak Abasi a-asañake akedʌk ke se Abasi akemek asọọñọ ada, <verse eid="ROM 9:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 9:12" />itooho ke utom ado ato ke anye a-akoodo, emaedọkkọ Ribeka ebo, “Andikpon ñkan adiinam ñkpọ inọ andisịb ñkan.” <verse eid="ROM 9:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 9:13" />Kpa naña ewet ate “Yekọb ke ami ñkema, ado Isọ ke ami ñkesua.”<verse eid="ROM 9:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 9:14" />Nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiitañ? Nte Abasi inenne? Idooho ntoro! <verse eid="ROM 9:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 9:15" />Sia anye amaadọkkọ Moses ate,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:15">“Ami ñyaatua awo se ami ñyem aditua mbọm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:15">ndin ñnyʌñ ñkop udʌk mbaña awo se ami ñyem adikop udʌk.”<verse eid="ROM 9:15" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 9:16" />Ke ntoro, idooho ke udọñ me adudu awo, ado ato ke mbọm Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 9:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 9:17" />Sia e-edọkkọ Fero ke ikọ Abasi ate: “Ami ñkudịppe fiin nnịm nnọ kpa ntak ami, nọ ami uwọt fiin adudu mmi ke idem mfo nọ anyịñ mmi asuana ke afịd ederimbod.” <verse eid="ROM 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 9:18" />Ke ntoro Abasi anie mbọm abaña awo se anye ayem inie mbọm mbaña, ndin anye anyʌñ asọñesịd ye awo a-anye ayemme isọñesịd.<verse eid="ROM 9:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 9:19" />Keed ke atu ndufo ayambo miin: “Ndin nsoo ido ntak a-Abasi asʌkkọ akịt ndudue ke idem ñnyịn? Sia anie ikan ibiọọñọ uduak amọ?” <verse eid="ROM 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 9:20" />Ado afo ado anie, ado awo, adifaaña ikọ ye Abasi? Nte ñkpọ se ebot ayaabo andibod anye ate, “Ntak a-afo ambotto miin ntom-o?” <verse eid="ROM 9:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 9:21" />Nte abodabañ inieghe unen adikama ukem eboho aduañ mbot nsio-nsio ñkpọ, ubaak asaña-asaña ñkpọ ubaak ado adaña-adaña ñkpọ?<verse eid="ROM 9:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 9:22" />Yak diin ise, adieke Abasi akpemekke adiwọt ifiobesịd amọ anyʌñ anam ediọọñọ adudu amọ, ado ayọ ye ekamba ime mme ñkpọ e-enọọhọ anye ifiobesịd, a-anye akebeeñeke idem adisoobo-o? <verse eid="ROM 9:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 9:23" />Ñko, akpedo anye akenam ami adiyaara ekamba ubọọñ amọ nnọọ ñkpọ a-anye anieghe mbọm abaña, a-anye akebakka adiọñ anịm adinọ ubọọñ, <verse eid="ROM 9:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 9:24" />kpa ñnyịn, a-anye amaakekoot, idooho ke atu mme Yuu ikpọọñ ado mme Gentile ñko-o? <verse eid="ROM 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 9:25" />Kpa naña anye abo ke ñwed Hosie:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:25">“Ami ñyaakoot ammọ ‘ikọd mmi’ akpesʌkado ammọ imiidooho ikọd mmi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:25">ami ñkọ ñyaakoot anye ‘ima mmi’ akpesʌkado a-anye imiidooho ima mmi,”<verse eid="ROM 9:25" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 9:26" />ndin,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:26">“Ayaatịppe kpa ke itie e-ekebooho ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:26">‘Ndufo idooho ikọd mmi’</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:26">eyaekoot ammọ ‘nditọ aduuwem Abasi.’ ”<verse eid="ROM 9:26" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 9:27" />Aisaiya a-abọọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio abaña Isrel:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:27">“Akpesʌkado ibad nditọ Isrel ewakka nte ntan ke mben inyañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:27">mme ñyọhọnsʌhọ kpọd ke ediinyaaña.<verse eid="ROM 9:27" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 9:28" />Sia Abọọñ ayaasọsọp anam ubiideikpe</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:28">amọ ke ederimbod ama ataa afịd-afịd.”<verse eid="ROM 9:28" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 9:29" />Ado naña nte Aisaiya amaaketatañ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:29">“Imiikpikidooho Abọọñ Andikponñkan akeyaak nsʌhọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:29">ubon anịm inọọ ñnyịn,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:29">ñnyịn ikpikiba nte Sọdọm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:29">ñnyịn ikpikiba nte Komora.”<verse eid="ROM 9:29" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Unana Mbuọdidem Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ROM 9:30" />Nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiitañ? Idiibo ke mme Gentile, i-idiikikeeneke adinenido, ebọ adinenido a-atooho ke mbuọdidem; <verse eid="ROM 9:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ROM 9:31" />ado mbon Isrel, e-ekekeeneke mbed adinenido, ikanna inie anye? <verse eid="ROM 9:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ROM 9:32" />Ke nsoo ntak? Ke ntak adooho ammọ ikiyemme adinenido ito mbuọdidem ado nte ebo ke ekebọ eto utom. Ammọ emaetuak ukod ke itiad iduọ enyʌñ eduọññọ. <verse eid="ROM 9:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ROM 9:33" />Nte naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 9:33">“Se, ami mmenịm itiad ke Saiyọn a-anamma nọ mme awo etuak ukod,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:33">ye ekamba itiad a-anamma mme awo eduọññọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 9:33">ndin awo a-anịmme anye ke akpanikọ idiikịtte abuud ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="ROM 9:33" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="ROM 10" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 10:1" />Nditọete, se ido udọñ esịd mmi ye akam a-ami mbọññọ nnọ Abasi mbaña nditọ Isrel ado yak ammọ ekpekap ebọ adinyaaña. <verse eid="ROM 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 10:2" />Sia mmekan aditie ntiense mbaña ammọ nte ke ammọ e-enie udọñ enọ Abasi, ado udọñ ammọ isañake ye ifiọk. <verse eid="ROM 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 10:3" />Sia ammọ imiikidiọọñọke adinenido Abasi ado eyem adikeene usʌñ a-ammọ, ammọ ikisuuhọ iwuod inọ adinenido Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 10:4" />Krais ado utịd afịd mbed nọ ato do adinenido aba anọ afịd awo se inịm ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="ROM 10:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 10:5" />Moses awet ami abaña usʌñ adinenido a-asañake ke mbed: “Awo a-anamma mme ñkpọ ami adiidu uwem akeene mme mbed ami.” <verse eid="ROM 10:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 10:6" />Ado adinenido a-atooho ke mbuọdidem abo ntom: “Kuubo ke esịd mfo, ‘Anie adiidọọk ika hefịn?’ ” (a-adooho, adisuuhọ Krais itie) <verse eid="ROM 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 10:7" />“me, ‘Anie adiitịkke idʌk ke ntotəño itie?’ ” (a-adooho, adibenne Krais nsio ke ñkpa). <verse eid="ROM 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 10:8" />Ado nsoo ke anye atañ? “Ikọ u-ukpere fiin; asịne ke inua mfo ye ke esịd mfo,” a-adooho, ikọ mbuọdidem a-ñnyịn ikwọrọke ibaña: <verse eid="ROM 10:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 10:9" />Adieke afo atañña ke inua mfo abo ke, “Yisọs ado Abọọñ” ndin anyʌñ anịm ke esịd mfo ate ke Abasi amaanam anye aset ke ñkpa, afo ayaanie adinyaaña. <verse eid="ROM 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 10:10" />Sia ado ke esịd mfo ke afo anịm ke akpanikọ ndin anie unen, ñko ato ke inua mfo, afo ayaara mbuọdidem mfo ndin anie adinyaaña. <verse eid="ROM 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 10:11" />Nte ikọ Abasi atañña, “Awo keed akeedodo a-anịmme Yisọs ke akpanikọ idiikịtte asuenne ke nsi-nsi.” <verse eid="ROM 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 10:12" />Sia ukpʌhọde ibaaha ke ufọọd mme Yuu ye mme Gentile, ukem Abọọñ ado ado Abọọñ afịd awo a-adiọññọ afịd awo se ikoot anye ayọhọ-ayọhọ, <verse eid="ROM 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 10:13" />sia, “Afịd awo se ikoot anyịñ Abọọñ eyaebọkkọ.”<verse eid="ROM 10:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 10:14" />Die ke ammọ ediikan ikoot anye a-ammọ imiinịmme ke akpanikọ? Die ke ammọ ediikan inịm anye a-ammọ imiikoppo ñkpọ ibaña? Die ke ammọ ediikop ke ini awo se ikwọrọ ikọ Abasi inọ ammọ imiibaaha? <verse eid="ROM 10:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 10:15" />Die ke awo adiikwọrọ ke imiibọhọke edọdọñ ammọ? Kpa naña ewet, “Ñkpad mbon ado edatta eti etob edi ayaiya eti-eti!”<verse eid="ROM 10:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 10:16" />Ado idooho afịd nditọ Isrel ekenyịmme eti etob ami. Sia Aisaiya a-abo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, anie awo inịm mbʌk ñnyịn ke akpanikọ?” <verse eid="ROM 10:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 10:17" />Ke ntoro, mbuọdidem ato ke adikop etob, ndin adikop etob ato ikọ a-abañake Krais. <verse eid="ROM 10:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 10:18" />Ado ami mbịp, nte ammọ ikikoppo? Ke akpanikọ, ammọ emaekop:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 10:18">“Uyio ammọ amaawuọ adʌk afịd ederimbod,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 10:18">ikọ ammọ ñko amaawuọ utịd ederimbod.<verse eid="ROM 10:18" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 10:19" />Ñko mmaana mbịp: Ado nte ikinwañake Isrel? Akpa, Moses abo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 10:19">“Ami ñyaanam ndufo efịbe ufịb ebaña mbon i-imiidooho idịd;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 10:19">Ami ñyaanam ndufo eyat esịd ebaña idịd i-imiinieghe ndiọọñọidem.”<verse eid="ROM 10:19" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 10:20" />Ndin Aisaiya atañ uko-uko ate,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 10:20">“Mbon i-imiikiñyemme miin emaeñkịt;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 10:20">ami mmaayaara idem mmi nnọ mbon i-mmiikibịppe imbaña miin.”<verse eid="ROM 10:20" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 10:21" />Ado ke atuuhọ Isrel anye abo ntom ate,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 10:21">“Afịd usen ami mmaanyan ubọk mmi nnọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 10:21">mbon ntreutọñ ye mbon ukpọtiọ.”<verse eid="ROM 10:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="ROM 11" />
  <para style="s1">Ñyọhọnsʌhọ Ufọk Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 11:1" />Ami mbịp ndin mbo: Ado nte Abasi amaasịn ikọd amọ? Nwaaña nsa-o! Ami ndo awo Isrel ke idem mmi, nto ubon Ebraham, a-atooho ekpək Benyamin. <verse eid="ROM 11:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 11:2" />Abasi ikisịnne ikọd amọ a-anye amaaketo adiọọñọ. Ado nte ndufo idiọọñọke se ikọ Abasi abo ke itie ñwed keed abaña Elaiya, naña anye aketọt Abasi abaña ndiọiñkpọ Isrel ate: <verse eid="ROM 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 11:3" />“Abọọñ, ammọ e-ewoot mme prọfed mfo enyʌñ ewuut mme itie uwa mfo. Ami ikpọọñ ndisʌhọ, ndin ammọ esʌk eyem usʌñ adiñwot miin”? <verse eid="ROM 11:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 11:4" />Ndin nsoo ikido ibọọrọ a-Abasi akenọọhọ anye? “Ami mmenịm nnọ idem mmi awo tọsịn itiaba (7,000) i-imiitọọñọke edọñ inọ Baal.” <verse eid="ROM 11:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 11:5" />Kpa ntoro, ke ini ami, aba usadusʌhọ e-emekke eto mfọn. <verse eid="ROM 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 11:6" />Ndin adieke atooho ke mfọn, itooho aba ke utom; akpedo ntoro mfọn ikpidooho aba mfọn.<verse eid="ROM 11:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 11:7" />Nsoo ndin? Se nditọ Isrel ekenekke eyem, ammọ ikinieghe. Mme andimek ke atu ammọ ekenie, ado mbon ako emaesọñ esịd, <verse eid="ROM 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 11:8" />kpa naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 11:8">“Abasi amaanọ Sịbidịd ñkpeñenye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:8">anyen i-imiikikanna ikịt ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:8">ye utọñ i-imiikikanna ikop ikọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 11:8">tutu asịm usen mfịn.”<verse eid="ROM 11:8" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 11:9" />Ndin Defid abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 11:9">“Yak usọrọ ndia ammọ akappa afia ye mfịne,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:9">ado ñkpọiduọ ye ufen anọ ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 11:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 11:10" />Yak anyen akịm ammọ mbaak ammọ edikịt ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:10">ñko yak edem ammọ anʌhọ ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="ROM 11:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Ñkọk e-Efaahafaak</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 11:11" />Yak mmaana mbịp: Nte ammọ eketuak ukod nọ eduọññọ ndin ikanna idakka ida aba? Nwaaña nsa-o! Ato ke ndudue ammọ ke adinyaaña akedisịm mme Gentile nọ Isrel enie ufịb ebaña ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 11:12" />Ado adieke nnamndue ammọ akappake ado uwak inie anọ ederimbod, ndin ntakudua ammọ akappa ado uwak inie anọ mme Gentile, die ke mme edidiọñ ammọ adiikpon ke ini emaeben mme Yuu afịd esịn ke atu!<verse eid="ROM 11:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 11:13" />Ami ntañ ikọ ami inọ ndufo mme Gentile. Akpesʌkado a-ami ndooho isʌñutom nnọ mme Gentile, ami mmewọk inua ke ubiọñutom mmi <verse eid="ROM 11:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 11:14" />nọ ato do ami nnam kpa mme Yuu ñnyịn efịbe mme Gentile, nọ ñkan ñnyaaña usʌk mme Yuu. <verse eid="ROM 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 11:15" />Sia adieke adisịn ammọ akedatta adidiana keed asịn ke ederimbod, nsoo ndin ke adinyịmme ammọ adiido ikan uwem a-awuọhọ ato ñkpa? <verse eid="ROM 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 11:16" />Adieke ubaak usʌñuyo e-enọọhọ nte mme akpa mfịd asanake, ndin afịd itu amọ ado adisana; adieke adʌñ adooho adisana, mme ñkọk ñko enyʌñ edo ndisana.<verse eid="ROM 11:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 11:17" />Adieke usʌk mme ñkọk e-emaekebʌññọ ewuọ, ndin afo, ñkọm afo ado ọlif a-akọttọ ke akai ikọd, ekpukpịkke eben edian ke atu mme ñkọk mbon ñko, ndin afo a-akeene awuana idahami ke udeeme nduañ uwem a-atooho eti adʌñ ọlif, <verse eid="ROM 11:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 11:18" />ikiinam nte ndufo emefọn ekan mme ñkọk mbon ñko. Adieke enamma ntoro, ikere ntom ise: Ndufo inwamma adʌñ ado, ado adʌñ akappa inwam ndufo. <verse eid="ROM 11:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 11:19" />Ndin afo ayaabo, “Ekekpooño ñkọk esioño nọ emben miin edian.” <verse eid="ROM 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 11:20" />Yak ibo ke ado ntoro. Ado ekekpịkke ammọ esio ke ntak unana mbuọdidem, ndin afo ada ke mbuọdidem. Ke ntoro kuukokko idem, ado nie uteñe. <verse eid="ROM 11:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 11:21" />Sia adieke Abasi imiikifeene inọ mme ñkọk eto, anye iduufeene fiin ñko.<verse eid="ROM 11:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 11:22" />Kere ndin baña mfọn ye nsọñido Abasi: Nsọñido anọ mbon e-emaekeduọññọ, ado mfọnido unọ fiin, afo ukpukap ukaiso umʌm mfọnido amọ ukama. Mmiidooho ntoro eyaukpịkke fiin ñko esio. <verse eid="ROM 11:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 11:23" />Ndin adieke ammọ imiikaaha iso ke unana adinịm ke akpanikọ, eyaeben ammọ edian, sia Abasi akeme adiben ammọ mmaana ndian. <verse eid="ROM 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 11:24" />Ndin adieke ekukpịkkeke fiin esio ke uduud afai eto ọlif, ndin uben fiin edian ke eti uduud eto ọlif, die ndin ke mbon ami, mme ataa ñkọk ami, ke emaetịmme edidian ammọ ke eto ọlif, imiididianake mfọn-mfọn!<verse eid="ROM 11:24" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Eyaenyaaña Afịd Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 11:25" />Ami ñyemme ndufo enana ifiọk ebaña ndedịbe ñkpọ ami, nditọeka mmi ke Krais, mbaak ndufo idikokko idem: Nsọñiwuod nditọ Isrel adikpeene tutu afịd ibad mbon mme Gentile edʌk edi. <verse eid="ROM 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 11:26" />Ndin ke utọ usʌñ ami eyaenyaaña afịd Isrel. Kpa naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 11:26">“Andinyaaña adiito ke Saiyọn idi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:26">anye ayaawọññọ unana adidiọọñọ Abasi akpọñ Yekọb.<verse eid="ROM 11:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 11:27" />Ndin ami ado edioomo mmi ye ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:27">ke mmaaben idiọọkñkpọ ammọ mfep.”<verse eid="ROM 11:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 11:28" />Ke ntak eti etob, mme Yuu edoñño mme asua ke ntak mfo, ado ke ntak a-Abasi akemekke ammọ, ema ammọ ke ntak mme nsọbom ammọ, <verse eid="ROM 11:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 11:29" />sia awo ikemeke adisọọk mme enọ Abasi ye ikood amọ mfep. <verse eid="ROM 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ROM 11:30" />Kpa naña ndufo e-ekesọññọ iwuod ke ini ako ye Abasi ado idahami e-ebọ mbọm ke ntak ntịdutọñ ammọ, <verse eid="ROM 11:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ROM 11:31" />kpasʌk ntoro ammọ, ke ntak mbọm a-Abasi inọọhọ ndufo, etịt utọñ idahami<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11:31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed inieghe </char><char style="fq" closed="false">idahami</char></note> nọ ammọ ebọ mbọm Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 11:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ROM 11:32" />Sia Abasi ayaak afịd awo asịn ke ntịdutọñ nọ ato do anye anie mbọm anọ afịd ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 11:32" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Itooro Abasi</para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ROM 11:33" />O, ntotəño inie, aniọñ ye ifiọk Abasi!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:33">Die ke awo imiikanna iduuñọ mme ubiideikpe amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:33">mme usʌñ amọ a-akan se ekeme idiọọñọ.<verse eid="ROM 11:33" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ROM 11:34" />“Anie awo adiọọñọ akikere Abọọñ?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:34">Anie ado andinọ anye item?<verse eid="ROM 11:34" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ROM 11:35" />Akenaanam anie anọ Abasi ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:35">nọ Abasi adiinọ ammọ usiene?”<verse eid="ROM 11:35" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ROM 11:36" />Sia ato ke anye, aboiyo ke anye, afịd ñkpọ ebañña, ndin afịd ñkpọ enie anye.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 11:36">Yak ubọọñ anie anye ke nsi-nsi! Amen.<verse eid="ROM 11:36" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="ROM 12" />
  <para style="s1">Aduuwem Uwa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 12:1" />Ke ntoro, ami mmikpeiye ndufo, nditọeka ke Krais, ke ntak mbọm Abasi, nte yak enịm idem ndufo nte aduuwem uwa, a-asanake, a-anyʌññọ anem Abasi esịd, anye ami ado nnen-nnen ye eti usʌñ adikpono Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 12:2" />Ikiinañña ñkpọ ikeene naña ubonoñkpọ ederimbod aba, ado yak akikere ndufo akpəho ke adidu ufa uwem. Ndin ndufo eyaekan edomo enyʌñ enyịmme se ido uduak Abasi, eti ñkpọ Abasi, a-afọnnọ, anyʌñ anem anye esịd.<verse eid="ROM 12:2" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Unam Utom Ufọkabasi ke Nsuukidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 12:3" />Mfọn e-ennọọhọ miin anam ami ibo ndufo keedekeed: Ikiikịt idem ndufo nọ akpon akan naña akpenaa ndufo ekịt, ado ikap inie eti iwuod ye mfarakeidem, nọ asaña akekem ke udomo mbuọdidem a-Abasi inọọhọ ndufo keedekeed. <verse eid="ROM 12:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 12:4" />Sia kpa naña ñnyịn keedekeed inie abʌkidem keed ye uwak ndido, ndin mme ndido ami inieñeke ukem ubọkutom, <verse eid="ROM 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 12:5" />kpa ntoro ke Krais, akpesʌkado ñnyịn iwakka, ido Ikpọkidem keed, ndin afịd ñnyịn idoñño ndido inọ emọ-emọ. <verse eid="ROM 12:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 12:6" />Ñnyịn iminie nsio-nsio enọ, akeene mfọn a-Abasi inọọhọ ñnyịn keedekeed. Adieke enọ mfo adooho aditañ brọfesi, tañ nọ asaña akekem ke mbuọdidem mfo. <verse eid="ROM 12:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 12:7" />Adieke adooho adinam ñkpọ nnọọ awo, nam ñkpọ nọ awo; adieke adooho adikpeep ñkpọ, kpeep ñkpọ; <verse eid="ROM 12:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 12:8" />adieke adooho adinọ nsọọñọnda, ndin nọ nsọọñọnda; adieke adooho adinọ enọ, nọ ke ntadubọk, adieke adooho adidat usʌñ, dat usʌñ ke afịdesịd; adieke adooho aditua awo mbọm, nam ado ke inemesịd.<verse eid="ROM 12:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ima Anam Utom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 12:9" />Ima ana asaña ye akpanikọ. Isua se idiọọk; isọọñọ iyịre ke se ifọn. <verse eid="ROM 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 12:10" />Inam ñkpọ inọ emọ-emọ ke ima. Ikpono emọ-emọ ikan idem ndufo. <verse eid="ROM 12:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 12:11" />Ikiinana akpọsọñ udọñ, ado inie ekamba ufiob udọñ ke Sịbidịd, ke adinam ñkpọ nnọọ Abọọñ. <verse eid="ROM 12:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 12:12" />Ndufo idaara ke idodanyen, inie ime ke ini afanekọñ, inyʌñ ibọñ akam afịd ini. <verse eid="ROM 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 12:13" />Iwana inie ndufo ye mme ndisana ikọd Abasi e-ebaaha ke unana. Ikaa iso adifọn mfọn.<verse eid="ROM 12:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 12:14" />Idiọñ mbon i-ikọbọke ndufo, idiọñ ado ikiisuuñọ ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 12:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 12:15" />Idaara ye mbon e-edaarake, itua ye mbon e-etuañake. <verse eid="ROM 12:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 12:16" />Idʌñ ke emem ye emọ-emọ, ikiikịt idem, ado inyịmme adiwana ye mbon awo e-ebaaha ke usuuhọ itie. Ikiikokko idem.<verse eid="ROM 12:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 12:17" />Ikiidat idiọọk isio awo ndomokeed usiene idiọọk. Ikịt ibo ke emenam se ifọn ke anyen afịd awo. <verse eid="ROM 12:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 12:18" />Naña ndufo ekpekakan, idʌñ ke emem ye afịd awo. <verse eid="ROM 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 12:19" />Mme ndima ufan mmi, ikiisio awo usiene, ado iyaak ufañ inọ ifiobesịd Abasi, sia e-ewet: “Usiene annie miin; ami ñyaasio usiene,” Abọọñ abo. <verse eid="ROM 12:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 12:20" />Utu ke ado:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 12:20">“Adieke abiọọñ adọññọ asua mfo, nọ anye ndidia,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 12:20">adieke itọñ asatta anye, nọ anye ñkpọ anwọñ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 12:20">Ke adinam ntom, afo ayaabək ufiob ukañ ke iwuod amọ.”<verse eid="ROM 12:20" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 12:21" />Ikiiyak idiọọk ikan ndufo ubọk, ado idat nti ñkpọ ikan idiọọk ubọk.<verse eid="ROM 12:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="ROM 13" />
  <para style="s1">Usuukiwuod Nnọọ mme Adaiwuod</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 13:1" />Yak afịd awo esuuk iwuod enọ mme adaiwuod ukara, sia ukara ndomokeed ibaaha ibọhọke anye a-Abasi anịmme. Mme andikara e-ebaññake edoñño mbon se Abasi amaakemek. <verse eid="ROM 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 13:2" />Ke ntoro, awo a-anwanake ye ukara anwana ye ukara a-Abasi amaakenịm, ndin mbon se inam ntoro eyaedat ubiomikpe enọ idem ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 13:3" />Sia mme adaukara idoññoke ñkpọ ndịk inọ mbon e-enaññake nti ñkpọ, ado edoñño ñkpọndịk enọ mbon e-enaññake ndiọi ido. Ndufo emeyem ibọkkọ ndịk awo a-abaaha ke ukara? Inam se inen, ndin anye ayaitooro ndufo. <verse eid="ROM 13:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 13:4" />Sia awo a-abaaha ke ukara ado ayịnufọk Abasi ke ufọn ndufo. Ado adieke enamma idiọọk, ikop ndịk, sia anye ikamake akañkañ amọ ke unana ntak. Anye ado isʌñutom Abasi, ndin a-anie unen adimia anam idiọọkñkpọ ufen. <verse eid="ROM 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 13:5" />Ke ntoro, a-adot adisuuk iwuod nnọọ ukara, idooho ke ntak umia ufen ikpọọñ, ado ke ntak eti akikere esịd ñko.<verse eid="ROM 13:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 13:6" />Ami ñko ado ntak a-ndufo ekpeeghe etịbe abio, sia mbon ukara edoñño nditọutom Abasi, e-eyaaha afịd ini ammọ esịn ke utom ukara. <verse eid="ROM 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 13:7" />Inọ afịd awo se ndufo ekama ammọ: Adieke afo akamake taks, kpe taks, adieke akamake utịb akʌk abio, kpe; adieke adooho uteeñe, nọ uteeñe; adieke adooho ukpono, nọ ukpono.<verse eid="ROM 13:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ima Anam Mbed Ayọhọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 13:8" />Inaaha awo ndomokeed akamaisọn, ibọhọke isọn adika iso mma emọ-emọ, sia awo akeedodo a-amaaha awo mfen a-anịm afịd mbed. <verse eid="ROM 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 13:9" />Mme mbed e-ebooho, “Kuusịn efịbe,” “Kuuwot awo,” “Kuuyịp inọ,” “Kuusịn anyen ke ñkpọ awo,” ye mme mbed mfen akeedodo, ekọñọ ke ewʌhọ keed ami: “Ma mbọhọidʌñ mfo nte idem mfo.” <verse eid="ROM 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 13:10" />Ima inamma mbọhọidʌñ idiọọk. Ke ntak ami ima ado adinịm mbed ayọhọ-ayọhọ.<verse eid="ROM 13:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Usen a-Akpere</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 13:11" />Ndin inam ami, sia ndufo emediọọñọ ini ami. Ini ado ami a-anaaha ndufo edemme ke idab, sia adinyaaña ñnyịn a-akpere idahami akan idaha a-ñnyịn ikitọọñọke inịm ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ROM 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 13:12" />Ayio ayaasiere, ubakusen akpere. Ndin yak ñnyịn ikpọñ mme ndiọiñkpọ ekịm, iben afọñ ekọñ unwana isịne ke idem. <verse eid="ROM 13:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 13:13" />Yak ñnyịn idu uwem a-afọnnọ nte iba ke uweemeayio, idooho ke unana mfadidem ye ukpa mmịn, idooho ke abʌd-abʌd ido, me use me mbubiam eduuwem, idooho ke utọk me ke ufịb. <verse eid="ROM 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 13:14" />Ado iben Abọọñ Yisọs Krais isịne ke idem ndufo, ndin ikiikere adiyʌkkọ mme ndiọi udọñ abʌkidem ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 13:14" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="ROM 14" />
  <para style="s1">Mbon Mmemidem ye mme Ñkpọsọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 14:1" />Idaara, ikiisat awo a-mbuọdidem amọ amemme, ndin ikiifaaña ye anye ibaña ñkpọ se isịne mfaaña. <verse eid="ROM 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 14:2" />Mbuọdidem awo keed akeme adiyak anye adia ñkpọ keed akeedodo, ado awo mfen a-mbuọdidem amọ amemme, adia mme ñkọñ kpọd. <verse eid="ROM 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 14:3" />Awo a-adiaha afịd ñkpọ inaaha ase awo mfen i-imiidiaha ntoro ke ndek, ndin awo i-imiidiaha afịd ñkpọ inaaha abiideikpe anọ awo a-adiaha, sia adooho Abasi isatta ammọ ndomokeed. <verse eid="ROM 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 14:4" />Afo ado anie adibiide ikpe nnọọ ayịnufọk awo mfen? Eteufọk amọ ikpọọñ akeme ibiere ikpe nnọọ anye, idooho afo. Ndin ke unwam Abasi ammọ eyaenam se ifọn, sia Abọọñ akeme inam ammọ enam se ifọn.<verse eid="ROM 14:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 14:5" />Awo keed akere ke usen keed a-asana akan usen mfen; awo mfen akere ke afịd usen ado ukem-ukem, awo keedekeed ana atʌm akere se ifọn ke esịd amọ. <verse eid="ROM 14:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 14:6" />Awo a-adatta usen keed nte akpan usen, anam ado anọ Abọọñ. Awo a-ataaha unam, ata anọ Abọọñ sia anye anọ Abasi ekọọm; ndin awo i-imiitaaha, anam anọ Abọọñ anyʌñ anọ Abasi ekọọm. <verse eid="ROM 14:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 14:7" />Sia ibaaha awo ndomokeed a-aduuho uwem anọ idem amọ ikpọọñ, inyʌññọ iba awo ndomokeed akpaaha anọ idem ñnyịn ikpọọñ. <verse eid="ROM 14:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 14:8" />Adieke ñnyịn iduuho uwem, ñnyịn idu inọ Abọọñ, ndin adieke ñnyịn ikpaaha, ñnyịn ikpa inọ Abọọñ. Ke ntoro adooho ñnyịn idu uwem anyʌññọ ado ikpaakpa, Abọọñ inie ñnyịn. <verse eid="ROM 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 14:9" />Akedo ke ntak ami ke Krais akekpa ndin atịmme aset ke ñkpa nọ ato do anye adido Abọọñ mme akpañkpa ye mme aduuwem.<verse eid="ROM 14:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 14:10" />Ndin, ntak a-afo akpeeghe ikpe anọọ ayịneka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ayịneka awodeen me awonwaan ada anọ </char><char style="ft" closed="false">(<char style="tl">adelfọs</char>) anyʌññọ awuọñọ mbon e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, me awodeen me awonwaan, ke atu mbon ubon Abasi; se ñko ke Rom 14:13, 15, 21.</char></note> mfo ke Krais-e? Nsoo inam afo ase ammọ ke mbio? Toiyo ke afịd ñnyịn iyaida ke ebekpo ubiideikpe Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 14:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 14:11" />E-ewet ebo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 14:11">“ ‘Ke adaña nte ami nduuho uwem,’ Abọọñ atañ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 14:11">‘afịd edọñ eyaetọọñọ ennọ miin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 14:11">afịd edeme eyaetañ ikọ ntiense ebaña Abasi.’ ”<verse eid="ROM 14:11" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 14:12" />Ke ntoro ñnyịn keedekeed iyainam ibad adinam ñnyịn inọ Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 14:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 14:13" />Ndin yak ñnyịn itre adibiom emọ-emọ ikpe. Utu ke ado, biere ke esịd mfo aditre adinịm ñkpọiduọ me ubiọọñọ ke usʌñ ayịneka mfo ke Krais. <verse eid="ROM 14:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 14:14" />Nte awo a-abaaha ke Abọọñ Yisọs, ami mmenịm ayọhọ-ayọhọ ke ndidia ndomokeed idegheke ke idem amọ. Ado adieke awo ndomokeed adatta ñkpọ ndomokeed ke ndek, ñkpọ ado ado ndek anọ anye. <verse eid="ROM 14:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 14:15" />Adieke ayịneka mfo ke Krais abaaha ke mfəhọ ke ntak ñkpọ se afo adia, afo unamma aba ke ima akpesʌk akaiso adia. Kuuyak ato ke ntak ndidia, afo aben nsobo asọk ayịneka mfo a-Krais akekpaaha anọ. <verse eid="ROM 14:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 14:16" />Ke ntoro kuuyak etañ idiọọk ikọ ebaña se afo adiọọñọ ke ado eti ñkpọ. <verse eid="ROM 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 14:17" />Sia abioubọọñ Abasi ikọñọke ke udia ñkpọ ye unwọn ñkpọ, ado akọñọ ke adinenido, emem ye idadesịd ke Adisana Sịbidịd, <verse eid="ROM 14:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 14:18" />sia awo akeedodo a-anamma ñkpọ anọ Krais ke usʌñ ami a-anem Abasi esịd, mme awo enyʌñ ekpono anye.<verse eid="ROM 14:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 14:19" />Yak ñnyịn ndin idomo ukeme adinam se idiidat emem idi inyʌñ inwam ke adisọọñọ emọ-emọ idem. <verse eid="ROM 14:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 14:20" />Ikiibiat ubọkutom Abasi ke ntak ndidia. Afịd ndidia asana, ado ifọnnọ awo adidia ñkpọ se idiinam awo mfen atuak ukod aduọ. <verse eid="ROM 14:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 14:21" />A-afọn awo aditre adita unam me adinwọñ mmịn me adinam ñkpọ mfen a-adiinam ayịneka amọ ke Krais akọbọ aduọ.<verse eid="ROM 14:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 14:22" />Ndin se afo anịm ke akpanikọ abaña mme ñkpọ ami yak ado ke ufọọd mfo ye Abasi. Afọfọn anọ awo i-imiibiommo idem amọ ikpe ato ke se anye anyịmme abo ke afọn. <verse eid="ROM 14:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 14:23" />Ado awo akeedodo a-anieghe eyịghe ke esịd, e-ebiom anye ikpe adieke anye adiaha, sia adidia amọ itooho mbuọdidem, ndin afịd ñkpọ se i-imiitooho mbuọdidem ado idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="ROM 14:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="ROM 15" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 15:1" />Ñnyịn mbon se isọñ idem akpena iyọ ye mbon mmemidem utu ke ñnyịn inem idem ñnyịn esịd. <verse eid="ROM 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 15:2" />Ñnyịn keedekeed akpena inam esịd anem mme mbọhọidʌñ ñnyịn ke adiyem ufọn ammọ ye adisọọñọ ammọ idem ke mbuọdidem. <verse eid="ROM 15:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 15:3" />Sia Krais ke idem amọ ikinamma ñkpọ se inem idem amọ esịd, ado nte naña ewet: “Mme usọñanyen a-mbon awo usọññọ fiin ekappa enduọññọ miin ke idem.” <verse eid="ROM 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 15:4" />Sia afịd ñkpọ se ekewet ke mme usen edem, ekewet adikpeep ñnyịn, nọ ato do ato ke ukpeeb adinie ime ye nsọọñọidem ke ikọ Abasi a-ammọ inọọhọ ñnyịn, ñnyịn inie idodanyen.<verse eid="ROM 15:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 15:5" />Yak Abasi a-anọọhọ awo ukeme adiyọ ye adisọọñọ mbon mfen idem inọ ndufo ukem esịd adibono ke ima naña Krais Yisọs akenie, <verse eid="ROM 15:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 15:6" />nọ ato ke esịd keed ye uyio keed ndufo ekeme adinọ Abasi ye Ete Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais ubọọñ.<verse eid="ROM 15:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 15:7" />Inyịmme emọ-emọ, naña Krais akinyịmme ndufo, nọ ato do enọ Abasi itooro. <verse eid="ROM 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 15:8" />Sia ami ntañ inọ ndufo ke Krais akappa ado ayịnufọk anọ mme Yuu ke ntak akpanikọ Abasi, nọ esọọñọ mme enwọñọ e-ekenamma enọ mme nsọbom mme Yuu, <verse eid="ROM 15:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 15:9" />ñkọ, nọ anam mme Gentile etooro Abasi ebaña mbọm amọ. Nte ewette:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 15:9">“Ke ntoro ami ñyautooro fiin ke atu mme Gentile;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 15:9">ñyaakwọ ikwọ itooro nnọ anyịñ mfo.”<verse eid="ROM 15:9" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 15:10" />Ñko anye amaana atañ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 15:10">“Idaara, ndufo mme Gentile, ye ikọd amọ.”<verse eid="ROM 15:10" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 15:11" />Ndin emaana ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 15:11">“Itooro Abọọñ, afịd ndufo mme Gentile,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 15:11">yak afịd awo enekke etooro anye.”<verse eid="ROM 15:11" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 15:12" />Ndin Aisaiya amaana atañ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 15:12">“Adʌñ Yesi ayaawuọ ada,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 15:12">anye a-adiidakka ida idikaara ke afịd mme idịd;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 15:12">mme Gentile ediinie idodanyen ito anye.”<verse eid="ROM 15:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 15:13" />Yak Abasi idodanyen iyọhọ ndufo ye afịd idadesịd ye emem naña ndufo edot anyen ke anye, nọ ndufo ekpesʌk eyọhọ ye idodanyen ke adudu Adisana Sịbidịd.<verse eid="ROM 15:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl, Akwọrọikọ Nnọọ mme Gentile</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 15:14" />Nditọeka mmi ke Krais, ami ke idem mmi mmenịm nte, ke ndufo ke idem ndufo emeyọhọ ye eti ido, emeyọhọ ye ifiọk enyʌñ enie ukeme adikpeep emọ-emọ ñkpọ. <verse eid="ROM 15:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 15:15" />Ado ami mmiwet ndufo ataa uko-uko mbaña mme uwọdñkpọ, adimaana itoiyo ndufo ke abaña mme ñkpọ ami akañ mfen, ke ntak mfọn a-Abasi annọọhọ miin <verse eid="ROM 15:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 15:16" />adido akwọrọikọ Krais Yisọs nnọọ mme Gentile. Anye amannọ miin iso utom nte aku adisuan eti etob Abasi, nọ ato do mme Gentile ekpekappa ñkpọ uwa anemme Abasi esịd a-Adisana Sịbidịd adiọññọ anọ Abasi.<verse eid="ROM 15:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 15:17" />Ke ntak ado ami mmetooro Krais Yisọs ke utom a-ami nnamma nnọ Abasi. <verse eid="ROM 15:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 15:18" />Ami ndiidomoke aditañ ñkpọ ndomokeed ibọhọke se Krais anam ama anto miin ke adidat mme Gentile usʌñ nọ ammọ esuuk iwuod enọ Abasi ato ke se ami ntañ ñnyʌñ nnam, <verse eid="ROM 15:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 15:19" />ke adudu ye mme idiọọñọ ye mme utịppeñkpọ, a-atooho ke adudu Sịbidịd Abasi. Ndin tọọñọ ke Yeruselem tutu akanna akewuọ Ilirikum, ami mmesuan etob eti mbʌk Krais ayọhọ-ayọhọ. <verse eid="ROM 15:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 15:20" />Asido udọñ mmi adikwọrọ eti etob Krais ke itie nte awo miikidiọọñọke Krais kpaanam, mbaak ami ndibọp ndot ke itiad idakisọñ awo mfen. <verse eid="ROM 15:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 15:21" />Ado, naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ROM 15:21">“Mbon a-awo imiikidọkkọke ibaña anye eyaekịt,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ROM 15:21">ndin mbon i-imiikikoppo eyaediọọñọ.”<verse eid="ROM 15:21" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 15:22" />Ami ado ntak ubiọọñọ mmi uwak ini adidi ndikịt ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 15:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Anam Akikere Adika Rom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 15:23" />Ado sia mme itie mfen ibaaha se ami nnam utom ke mme ñkanñkʌk umi, ñko sia mmaanenie udọñ ke uwak isua adidise ndufo, <verse eid="ROM 15:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 15:24" />mmenie akikere adinam ntoro ke mmaaka Speen. Ami mmenie idodanyen adidise ndufo ke idaha ndiiboiyo do, nọ ndufo eñnyaaña miin ke isañ mmi, sia mmaakop inem ke atu ndufo ke etək ini. <verse eid="ROM 15:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 15:25" />Ado idahami, ami mba ke usʌñ adika Yeruselem adinam utom nnọọ ikọd Abasi ke udo. <verse eid="ROM 15:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 15:26" />Sia Masidonia ye Akaya emaenem esịd adikeene ntịp etịbe ñnwam mme uweene ke atu mme ndisana ikọd Abasi ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="ROM 15:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 15:27" />Ammọ emaenem esịd adinam ami, sia ke akpanikọ ado isʌñ ke ammọ ekama ikọd Abasi ke Yeruselem. Sia adieke mme Gentile ewanake ke mme adidiọñ Sịbidịd mme Yuu, ammọ ñko ekama mme Yuu isọn ke adiwuana inie ederimbod ammọ ye mme Yuu. <verse eid="ROM 15:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ROM 15:28" />Ndin ke ami mmaakekweeñe iso utom ami, ñnyʌñ ntʌm ndiọọñọ ke ammọ e-ebọ enọ ami, ami ñyaakaa Speen ñnyʌñ mboiyo ndise ndufo. <verse eid="ROM 15:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ROM 15:29" />Ami mmediọọñọ ke mmaadi ibịne ndufo, ndiidi ke ayọhọ adidiọñ Krais.<verse eid="ROM 15:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ROM 15:30" />Ami mmikpeiye ndufo, nditọeka ke Krais ke ntak Abọọñ Yisọs Krais ye ke ima Sịbidịd, nte ediana ye ami ke anwan ami ke adibọñ akam nnọọ Abasi ke iwuod mmi. <verse eid="ROM 15:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ROM 15:31" />Ibọñ akam ibo eñnyaaña miin ke Yudia esio ke ubọk mbon i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ, ñko nọ ikọd Abasi ke Yeruselem ebọ enọ a-ami mbenne ñka do ke inemesịd, <verse eid="ROM 15:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ROM 15:32" />nọ ato do ke uduak Abasi ami ndi ibịne ndufo ke inemesịd, ñnyʌñ mbọ nduọkadudu ke ufọọd ndufo. <verse eid="ROM 15:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ROM 15:33" />Yak Abasi emem aba ye afịd ndufo. Amen.<verse eid="ROM 15:33" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <chapter eid="ROM 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="ROM 16" />
  <para style="s1">Akpọ-akpọ Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ROM 16:1" />Ami mmenọ ayịneka awonwaan ñnyịn Fibi, a-adooho dikịn<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Se ñko utom dikịn ke Filipai 1:1 ye 1 Timoti 3:8, 12</char></note> ufọkabasi ke Senkre isọk ndufo. <verse eid="ROM 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ROM 16:2" />Ndufo ibọ anye ke Abọọñ ke usʌñ a-adotto ke se mme ndisana awo ekpenam, inyʌñ inọ anye unwam akeedodo a-anye akpeyemme, sia anye ado unwam anọ uwak awo, ye ami ñko.<verse eid="ROM 16:2" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ROM 16:3" />Ikọọm Prisila<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Greek </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Priska</char><char style="ft" closed="false">asʌk ado </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Prisila</char></note> ye Akwila, mme nsaña utom mmi ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="ROM 16:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ROM 16:4" />Ammọ emaenyịmme adiduọọk uwem ammọ ke ntak mmi. Idooho ami ikpọọñ, ado afịd ufọkabasi mme Gentile ekọọm ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 16:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ROM 16:5" />Inyʌñ ikọọm ufọkabasi e-esisooboke ke ufọk ammọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:5">Ikọọm adima ufan mmi Ebenetus, a-akedooho akpa awo se ikikappa esịd ikeene Krais ke ñkanñkʌk Esia.<verse eid="ROM 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ROM 16:6" />Ikọọm Mmeri, a-akesịnne ifịk anam utom inọọ ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 16:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ROM 16:7" />Ikọọm Andronikus ye Yunia, mme nditọete mmi mme Yuu e-ekebaaha ke ñkpakọb ye ami. Ammọ edo mme awuọiso ke atu mme abọsịd, emaenyʌñ ediọọñọ Krais mbemiso ami.<verse eid="ROM 16:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ROM 16:8" />Ikọọm Ampliatus, adima ufan mmi ke Abọọñ.<verse eid="ROM 16:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ROM 16:9" />Ikọọm Ubanus, awo nsaña utom ñnyịn ke Krais, ye ataa adima ufan mmi Stakis.<verse eid="ROM 16:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ROM 16:10" />Ikọọm Apeles, e-emaekedomo ekịt ke nsuukiwuod amọ nnọọ Krais afọn.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:10">Ikọọm mbon e-etooho ufọk Aristobulus.<verse eid="ROM 16:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ROM 16:11" />Ikọọm Herọdiọn, awo Yuu nte ami.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:11">Ikọọm ikọd ufọk Nasisọs e-ebaññake ke Abọọñ.<verse eid="ROM 16:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ROM 16:12" />Ikọọm Trifena ye Trifosa, mme ibaan e-enamma akpọsọñ utom ke Abọọñ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:12">Ikọọm adima ufan mmi Pesis, awonwaan mfen a-anamma akpọsọñ utom ke Abọọñ.<verse eid="ROM 16:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ROM 16:13" />Ikọọm Rufọs e-emekke ke Abọọñ, ye eka amọ, a-adooho eka annọ miin ñko.<verse eid="ROM 16:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ROM 16:14" />Ikọọm Asinkritus, Flekọn, Hemas, Patrobas, Emas, ye mme nditọeka ke Krais mbon ñko e-ebaññake ye ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 16:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ROM 16:15" />Ikọọm Filọlọkus, Yulia, Nerus ye ayịneka amọ awonwaan, ye Olimpas ye afịd ndisana ikọd Abọọñ e-ebaññake ye ammọ.<verse eid="ROM 16:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ROM 16:16" />Ikọọm emọ-emọ ke adisana ntʌminua.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:16">Afịd mme ufọkabasi Krais edọñ ekọọm.<verse eid="ROM 16:16" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ROM 16:17" />Ami mmibeeñe ndufo nditọeka ke Krais, aditịñ anyen nse mbon e-esịnne ubakka enyʌñ enịm ñkpọiduọ ke usʌñ ndufo i-imiisañake ke ukpeeb a-ndufo ebọọhọ. Idiañña nsaña ikpọñ ammọ. <verse eid="ROM 16:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ROM 16:18" />Sia utọ ibon ado inamma ñkpọ inọ Abọọñ Krais, ado enam enọ idiọọk itọñ ammọ. Ke nneminua utañ ikọ ye ntiik, ammọ ebiaña mbon e-enieghe mfefeere esịd. <verse eid="ROM 16:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ROM 16:19" />Afịd awo e-ekop ebaña nsuukiwuod ndufo, ndin ami mmekop ayọhọ inemesịd ibaña ndufo. Ado ami ñyem ndufo ediọọñọ se ifọn ndin enyʌñ enana ndudue ke se ido idiọọk.<verse eid="ROM 16:19" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ROM 16:20" />Abasi emem ayaasọp anuak Setan ke idak mkpad ndufo.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="ROM 16:20" />
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:20">Yak mfọn Abọọñ Yisọs aba ye ndufo.<verse eid="ROM 16:20" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ROM 16:21" />Timoti awo nsaña utom mmi, a-adọñ ekọọm inọ ndufo, ukem ñko ye Lusiọs, Yasọn ye Sosipata ñko e-edoññoke Yuu nte ñnyịn.<verse eid="ROM 16:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ROM 16:22" />Ami, Tetius, andiwet ñwedetob ami mmikọọm ndufo ke Abọọñ.<verse eid="ROM 16:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ROM 16:23" />Kayọs, a-ami ye afịd ufọkabasi idiaha ufọn ukama isen amọ, a-adọñ ekọọm inọ ndufo.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ROM 16:23">Erastus, a-adooho adaiwuod ke utom abio, ye ayịneka ñnyịn Kwaatus, e-edọñ ekọọm inọ ndufo ñko.<verse eid="ROM 16:23" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ROM 16:24" />Yak mfọn Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais aba ye afịd ndufo. Amen.<verse eid="ROM 16:24" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ROM 16:25" />Ndin yak nsinsi ubọọñ anie anye a-akanna inọọ ndufo nsọọñọnda ke abaña eti etob ye se ñkwọrọ mbaña Yisọs Krais, naña asaña akekem ke adiyaara ndedịbe akpanikọ e-ekedịppedịp ke mme ayio edem a-amaakeboiyo, <verse eid="ROM 16:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ROM 16:26" />ado idahami eyaara enyʌñ enam ediọọñọ eto ke se mme prọfed ekewet, a-atooho ke ewʌhọ nsi-nsi Abasi, nọ ato do afịd awo ekpenịm ikọ Abasi enyʌñ esuukiwuod enọ anye ke mbuọdidem. <verse eid="ROM 16:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ROM 16:27" />Yak ato Yisọs Krais itooro anie ukweeñe adiọọñọñkpọ Abasi ke nsi-nsi! Amen.<verse eid="ROM 16:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ROM 16" />
</usx>